(ns eve.host-completion
  "jank's completion of its core to Clojure's, loaded first by eve.host (HOST-CONTRACT §10; measured on jank
   0.1-alpha, the jank 0.1-noble package of 2026-10-28, lane eve-jank J0/J1). What jank's core lacks, or answers
   otherwise, and eve needs:

   - defprotocol, deftype, defrecord, reify, extend-type, extend-protocol, extend, satisfies?, extends?: jank has
     none of them (no such macro or special form in its core or any shipped namespace). A protocol here is a table
     per method keyed by a value's type key (below), each method a fn of the arities its signature lists, caching
     the impl it found; extend writes the table. A deftype is one C++ object type compiled once in this namespace
     (eve_host::eve_obj: a tag naming the type, a vector of its fields), its methods extended to the tag; a mutable
     field holds a cell (volatile!) its factory makes, read by deref and set! by vreset! (as on clojerl and glojure),
     so such a type is built with ->T. T. and T__make are the factory too (jank keeps `T.` a plain symbol: a var of
     that name resolves it). A reify is an instance whose fields hold its closures, its tag made once for its form. A
     defrecord is a map carrying its type in metadata (:eve/record), so keyword lookup is jank's own.
   - type and class: a deftype instance answers its tag (a symbol); a record its record tag; everything else jank's
     own (a string naming the C++ type, e.g. \"persistent_vector\"). instance? reads the same.
   - = and hash: a type's own equivalence and hash answer for it once eve's types adapter names them
     (set-type-equality!, as glojure's) — jank's own = compares an opaque object by identity and never reaches a
     virtual (measured). The C++ hash does reach the hook, so a type is a usable key in jank's maps and sets
     by hash; equality there stays identity (jank's C++ path).
   - meta: jank's meta on an opaque object never returns (measured: a 60 s timeout); nil here for a type.
   - + - *: jank's add, sub and mul of two small integers (the int32 range) wrap at 32 bits (upstream defect 27;
     the first forms below); here they are checked — eve_arith's __builtin_*_overflow ops, throwing on i64
     overflow as the JVM's do (doc/arithmetic-overflow.md, the operator's 2026-11-07 decision), with jank's
     promoting ops left to +' -' *'. A loop local with an integer-literal init is
     boxed, so it holds a value past 2^31 through recur (upstream defect 21; the loop re-root below).
   - unchecked-*, byte, short: jank's core throws \"TODO: port\" from each (121 such names at 0.1); the fixed-width
     ones wrap here as the JVM's (over the promoting +' -' *' above). instance?, locking,
     hash-ordered-coll, hash-unordered-coll, mix-collection-hash, subseq, rsubseq, sequence, rseq, requiring-resolve,
     reversible?, indexed?, into-array, cast likewise.
   - A name interned into clojure.core here is seen by every namespace created after this one loads (measured), so
     the launcher requires eve.host-completion first (test/eve/runner/jank_main.jank).

   Re-rooted names hold for namespaces compiled after this one (alter-var-root on the core var: measured)."
  (:refer-clojure :exclude [extend mix-collection-hash hash-ordered-coll hash-unordered-coll locking])
  ;; Math, System, UUID are real source modules in this adapter (Math.jank,
  ;; System.jank, UUID.jank beside this file's tree): requiring them makes
  ;; them compiled modules in every graph that loads the completion, which
  ;; jank's AOT collector demands; the when-not synthesis blocks at the end
  ;; of this file remain as the fallback and skip when these have loaded.
  (:require [Math] [System] [UUID]))

;; The collector primed first: its heap grown to 64 MiB at once, so the load and a program's first allocations do not
;; collect at every few MiB of growth (Boehm's default start). GC_expand_hp in a static initializer runs as this
;; form's code is loaded (JIT) or at the binary's start (AOT); it initializes the collector if it is not yet.
(cpp/raw "
#include <gc.h>
namespace eve_gc { static bool const primed = [] { GC_expand_hp(static_cast<size_t>(64) << 20); return true; }(); }
")

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; + - * checked — first, so every form compiled after these lines takes them (this namespace's own included)
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; jank keeps an integer in the int32 range as a small_integer, and its add, sub and mul of two of them wrap at 32
;; bits (upstream defect 27, measured on jank 0.1-noble cf627abb…: (+ 2147483647 1) → -2147483648, (* 239 16777216)
;; → -285212672, (* 65535 65535) → -131071; through a fn's parameters and a long cast the same; an operand outside
;; the int32 range, inc, dec, quot, mod and the shifts are exact). eve's shared code counts on exact integers below
;; 2^53 — the portable XXH3-128's 32-bit limbs, and eve's type-ids through it (eve.deftype.type-id-steps-test: the
;; digest was the first step to leave, so every type-id differed on this host). So + - * were first pointed at
;; jank's own promoting ops, the ones +' -' *' call: exact below 2^63, promoting past it where the JVM throws.
;;
;; The operator's decision (2026-11-07; doc/arithmetic-overflow.md) closes that divergence: checked + - * throw
;; on i64 overflow on every host, as the JVM's do; +' -' *' promote; unchecked-* wrap. The binding here is
;; eve_arith's checked ops: for two i64 integers the C++ __builtin_*_overflow computes the value and its
;; overflow flag in one op (the flag-native seat's price, ≈0 — the proof lane's rows), and on overflow the op
;; answers the nil object, which no numeric op can legitimately answer, and the Clojure side throws — the
;; seat's throwable for an arithmetic fault is ex-info, as this completion's Divide by zero is. Any other
;; operands (a big integer, a double, a ratio) go through jank's promoting op, as +' does: the checked
;; semantics bind the i64 path only, exactly as the JVM's Numbers binds the long path only. inc and dec take
;; the same binding (the JVM's inc and dec throw too). jank exposes no Clojure-level checked op, so the
;; intrinsic lives in this cpp/raw, not upstream: nothing here patches jank.
(cpp/raw "
#include <jank/runtime/obj/nil.hpp>
#include <jank/runtime/core/math.hpp>
#include <jank/runtime/core/make_box.hpp>
namespace eve_arith {
  using namespace jank::runtime;
  /* the i64-valued integers: jank's small_integer (the int32 range) and integer boxes */
  static bool i64_integer(object_type const t) {
    return t == object_type::integer || t == object_type::small_integer;
  }
  bool is_big(object_ref const o) { return o.get_type() == object_type::big_integer; }
  object_ref checked_add(object_ref const l, object_ref const r) {
    if(i64_integer(l.get_type()) && i64_integer(r.get_type())) {
      jank::i64 res;
      if(__builtin_add_overflow(to_int(l), to_int(r), &res)) { return object_ref{}; }
      return make_box(res);
    }
    return promoting_add(l, r);
  }
  object_ref checked_sub(object_ref const l, object_ref const r) {
    if(i64_integer(l.get_type()) && i64_integer(r.get_type())) {
      jank::i64 res;
      if(__builtin_sub_overflow(to_int(l), to_int(r), &res)) { return object_ref{}; }
      return make_box(res);
    }
    return promoting_sub(l, r);
  }
  object_ref checked_mul(object_ref const l, object_ref const r) {
    if(i64_integer(l.get_type()) && i64_integer(r.get_type())) {
      jank::i64 res;
      if(__builtin_mul_overflow(to_int(l), to_int(r), &res)) { return object_ref{}; }
      return make_box(res);
    }
    return promoting_mul(l, r);
  }
  object_ref checked_negate(object_ref const x) {
    if(i64_integer(x.get_type())) {
      jank::i64 res;
      if(__builtin_sub_overflow(static_cast<jank::i64>(0), to_int(x), &res)) { return object_ref{}; }
      return make_box(res);
    }
    return promoting_sub(make_box(static_cast<jank::i64>(0)), x);
  }
  object_ref checked_inc(object_ref const x) {
    if(i64_integer(x.get_type())) {
      jank::i64 res;
      if(__builtin_add_overflow(to_int(x), static_cast<jank::i64>(1), &res)) { return object_ref{}; }
      return make_box(res);
    }
    return promoting_inc(x);
  }
  object_ref checked_dec(object_ref const x) {
    if(i64_integer(x.get_type())) {
      jank::i64 res;
      if(__builtin_sub_overflow(to_int(x), static_cast<jank::i64>(1), &res)) { return object_ref{}; }
      return make_box(res);
    }
    return promoting_dec(x);
  }
}
")

(defn checked-add
  "Two values added as clojure.core/+ means it (doc/arithmetic-overflow.md): jank's promoting answer, throwing
   ex-info \"integer overflow\" when two i64 integers overflow — this seat's ArithmeticException, as its Divide
   by zero is an ex-info."
  [l r]
  (let [res (cpp/eve_arith.checked_add l r)]
    (if (nil? res) (throw (ex-info "integer overflow" {})) res)))

(defn checked-sub [l r]
  (let [res (cpp/eve_arith.checked_sub l r)]
    (if (nil? res) (throw (ex-info "integer overflow" {})) res)))

(defn checked-mul [l r]
  (let [res (cpp/eve_arith.checked_mul l r)]
    (if (nil? res) (throw (ex-info "integer overflow" {})) res)))

(defn checked-negate [x]
  (let [res (cpp/eve_arith.checked_negate x)]
    (if (nil? res) (throw (ex-info "integer overflow" {})) res)))

(defn checked-inc [x]
  (let [res (cpp/eve_arith.checked_inc x)]
    (if (nil? res) (throw (ex-info "integer overflow" {})) res)))

(defn checked-dec [x]
  (let [res (cpp/eve_arith.checked_dec x)]
    (if (nil? res) (throw (ex-info "integer overflow" {})) res)))

;; The 2-, 3- and 4-ary calls inline to nested binary checked ops, left to right as the reduce below folds them
;; (a 3- or 4-ary call through the var's [x y & more] arity built a rest seq and reduced it: 591 ns against 359 for the
;; same arithmetic nested, measured /home/user/stage/probes/probe2.jank P2/P3); jank's analyzer reads :inline-arities
;; (core.jank's own + carries #{2}), so a 1-ary or 5+-ary call still reaches the var.
(defn- inline-fold [op]
  (fn* ([a b] (list op a b))
       ([a b c] (list op (list op a b) c))
       ([a b c d] (list op (list op (list op a b) c) d))))
(alter-meta! #'clojure.core/+ assoc :inline (inline-fold 'eve.host-completion/checked-add) :inline-arities #{2 3 4})
(alter-meta! #'clojure.core/- assoc :inline (inline-fold 'eve.host-completion/checked-sub) :inline-arities #{2 3 4})
(alter-meta! #'clojure.core/* assoc :inline (inline-fold 'eve.host-completion/checked-mul) :inline-arities #{2 3 4})
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/+
  (fn [_] (fn ([] 0)
              ([x] x)
              ([x y] (checked-add x y))
              ([x y z] (checked-add (checked-add x y) z))
              ([x y z w] (checked-add (checked-add (checked-add x y) z) w))
              ([x y z w & more] (reduce checked-add (checked-add (checked-add (checked-add x y) z) w) more)))))
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/-
  (fn [_] (fn ([x] (checked-negate x))
              ([x y] (checked-sub x y))
              ([x y z] (checked-sub (checked-sub x y) z))
              ([x y z w] (checked-sub (checked-sub (checked-sub x y) z) w))
              ([x y z w & more] (reduce checked-sub (checked-sub (checked-sub (checked-sub x y) z) w) more)))))
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/*
  (fn [_] (fn ([] 1)
              ([x] x)
              ([x y] (checked-mul x y))
              ([x y z] (checked-mul (checked-mul x y) z))
              ([x y z w] (checked-mul (checked-mul (checked-mul x y) z) w))
              ([x y z w & more] (reduce checked-mul (checked-mul (checked-mul (checked-mul x y) z) w) more)))))
(alter-meta! #'clojure.core/inc assoc :inline (fn* [x] (list 'eve.host-completion/checked-inc x)))
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/inc (fn [_] checked-inc))
(alter-meta! #'clojure.core/dec assoc :inline (fn* [x] (list 'eve.host-completion/checked-dec x)))
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/dec (fn [_] checked-dec))

;; / of two integers truncates on jank for every integer box ((/ 1 2) → 0, (/ 1N 2) → 0N; rationalize is a "TODO:
;; port" stub; measured: eve/probes/jank-ratio), so eve.numeric-tags-test's ratios never were ratios (5 FAILs). jank
;; has the ratio type: two integers divide here through obj::ratio::create — reduced, an integer when exact, a big
;; integer operand through native_big_integer (measured: probe4.jank, 2^128 denominators); any other operand jank's
;; own div. An integer zero divisor throws "Divide by zero" as the JVM does: jank's own integer div by zero is a C++
;; division by zero, which ends the process (SIGFPE, exit 136: measured).
(cpp/raw "
#include <jank/runtime/obj/ratio.hpp>
#include <jank/runtime/obj/big_integer.hpp>
#include <jank/runtime/core/math.hpp>
#include <jank/runtime/rtti.hpp>
namespace eve_arith {
  using namespace jank::runtime;
  static bool integral(object_type const t) {
    return t == object_type::integer || t == object_type::small_integer || t == object_type::big_integer;
  }
  static jank::native_big_integer as_big(object_ref const o) {
    if(o.get_type() == object_type::big_integer) { return expect_object<obj::big_integer>(o)->data; }
    return jank::native_big_integer(to_int(o));
  }
  /* an integer zero divisor, a big one compared as a big integer (jank's zero? of a 2^128 converts to i64 and throws
     \"out of range for i64 conversion\": measured, eve.numeric-tags-test's ratios-round-trip) */
  bool zero_divisor(object_ref const r) {
    auto const t(r.get_type());
    if(t == object_type::big_integer) { return expect_object<obj::big_integer>(r)->data == 0; }
    return integral(t) && to_int(r) == 0;
  }
  object_ref divide(object_ref const l, object_ref const r) {
    auto const lt(l.get_type()), rt(r.get_type());
    if(!integral(lt) || !integral(rt)) { return jank::runtime::div(l, r); }
    if(lt != object_type::big_integer && rt != object_type::big_integer) {
      return obj::ratio::create(static_cast<jank::i64>(to_int(l)), static_cast<jank::i64>(to_int(r)));
    }
    return obj::ratio::create(as_big(l), as_big(r));
  }
}
")

(defn- divide [l r]
  (if (cpp/eve_arith.zero_divisor r)
    (throw (ex-info "Divide by zero" {:numerator l}))
    (cpp/eve_arith.divide l r)))

(let [v (ns-resolve 'clojure.core '/)]
  (alter-meta! v dissoc :inline :inline-arities)
  (alter-var-root v (fn [_] (fn ([x] (divide 1 x))
                                ([l r] (divide l r))
                                ([l r & more] (reduce divide (divide l r) more))))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The object a deftype instance is: one C++ type for every eve type
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(cpp/raw "
#include <jank/runtime/object.hpp>
#include <jank/runtime/core.hpp>
#include <jank/runtime/core/make_box.hpp>
#include <jank/runtime/obj/nil.hpp>
#include <jank/runtime/obj/persistent_string.hpp>
#include <gc.h>
#include <jank/runtime/obj/detail/base_persistent_map.hpp>
#include <chrono>
/* A type hint on a parameter or a let binding is a C++ type to jank's analyzer (^long i makes i a native long,
   which works; an unknown name is \"Unable to find `bytes` within the global namespace\": measured). The names eve's
   shared code and tests hint with — eve.host's array casts, the JVM's root types, the JVM interfaces core.rrb-vector's
   EPL files name, and the eve types hinted by name — are aliases of object_ref here, so the hint is read and nothing
   is narrowed. A hint naming an eve type not listed here is a load error naming it: add it. */
using bytes = jank::runtime::object_ref; using shorts = jank::runtime::object_ref; using ints = jank::runtime::object_ref;
using longs = jank::runtime::object_ref; using floats = jank::runtime::object_ref; using doubles = jank::runtime::object_ref;
using objects = jank::runtime::object_ref; using booleans = jank::runtime::object_ref; using boolean = jank::runtime::object_ref;
using String = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Object = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Throwable = jank::runtime::object_ref;
using Exception = jank::runtime::object_ref; using ClassCastException = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Number = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Long = jank::runtime::object_ref;
using Integer = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Double = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Boolean = jank::runtime::object_ref;
using Character = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Comparable = jank::runtime::object_ref; using StringBuilder = jank::runtime::object_ref;
using LoggingSlabIO = jank::runtime::object_ref; using JvmSlabCtx = jank::runtime::object_ref; using EveArray = jank::runtime::object_ref;
using EveList = jank::runtime::object_ref; using EveVector = jank::runtime::object_ref; using EveHashMap = jank::runtime::object_ref;
using EveHashSet = jank::runtime::object_ref; using MmapAtom = jank::runtime::object_ref; using MmapAtomDomain = jank::runtime::object_ref;
using RSeq = jank::runtime::object_ref; using RRBChunkedSeq = jank::runtime::object_ref; using ObjArrayRow = jank::runtime::object_ref;
namespace java { namespace util { using Collection = jank::runtime::object_ref; using List = jank::runtime::object_ref;
  using ListIterator = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Iterator = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Map = jank::runtime::object_ref;
  using Set = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Date = jank::runtime::object_ref; using UUID = jank::runtime::object_ref; }
  namespace lang { using Object = jank::runtime::object_ref; using String = jank::runtime::object_ref; } }
namespace clojure { namespace lang { using ISeq = jank::runtime::object_ref; using IPersistentVector = jank::runtime::object_ref;
  using IPersistentMap = jank::runtime::object_ref; using IPersistentCollection = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Counted = jank::runtime::object_ref;
  using IFn = jank::runtime::object_ref; using IAtom = jank::runtime::object_ref; using IDeref = jank::runtime::object_ref;
  using Indexed = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Sequential = jank::runtime::object_ref; using IMapEntry = jank::runtime::object_ref;
  using ITransientCollection = jank::runtime::object_ref; using IEditableCollection = jank::runtime::object_ref; using IObj = jank::runtime::object_ref;
  using IHashEq = jank::runtime::object_ref; using IReduceInit = jank::runtime::object_ref; using IKVReduce = jank::runtime::object_ref;
  /* the rest of the :clj face's interface names (a vanilla deftype's specs and instance? tests name them):
     jank's analyzer reads clojure.lang.<Name> as a class, never as a var, so each needs its alias here */
  using Seqable = jank::runtime::object_ref; using ILookup = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Associative = jank::runtime::object_ref;
  using IPersistentSet = jank::runtime::object_ref; using IPersistentList = jank::runtime::object_ref; using IPersistentStack = jank::runtime::object_ref;
  using IMeta = jank::runtime::object_ref; using IReduce = jank::runtime::object_ref; using Reversible = jank::runtime::object_ref; } }
namespace eve_host {
  using namespace jank::runtime;
  /* the hooks are statics of JIT-compiled code, which the collector does not scan: registered as roots (without
     this the printer was collected under the object and a print crashed, at random: measured, J1) */
  static object_ref printer{ jank_nil };
  static object_ref equiv{ jank_nil };
  static object_ref hasher{ jank_nil };
  static object_ref lookup{ jank_nil };
  static object_ref dispatch{ jank_nil };
  static bool rooted{ false };
  static void root() { if(!rooted) { rooted = true; GC_add_roots(&printer, &printer + 1); GC_add_roots(&equiv, &equiv + 1); GC_add_roots(&hasher, &hasher + 1); GC_add_roots(&lookup, &lookup + 1); GC_add_roots(&dispatch, &dispatch + 1); } }
  static object_ref op(long n) { return make_box(static_cast<jank::i64>(n)); }
  struct eve_obj : object {
    static constexpr object_type obj_type{ object_type::opaque_box };
    /* jank 0.1 answers get, keyword invoke, get-in, contains?, seq, nth and a call through these virtuals when the
       object declares the behavior (its own maps do: call|get|find|seqable; measured for get and call:
       eve/probes/jank-xxh3/probe7.jank), so an eve value reaches its type's own ILookup, ISeqable, IIndexed and IFn
       through the lookup and dispatch hooks (F-3). A type without the protocol answers get's fallback as before,
       and throws for the others. */
    static constexpr object_behavior obj_behaviors{ object_behavior::get | object_behavior::find
                                                    | object_behavior::seqable | object_behavior::indexable
                                                    | object_behavior::call | object_behavior::compare };
    static constexpr bool pointer_free{ false };
    object_ref tag;
    object_ref fields;
    eve_obj(object_ref t, object_ref f) : object{ obj_type, obj_behaviors }, tag{ t }, fields{ f } {}
    /* a raw this is shifted into NaN space by the untagged_ptr constructor (oref.hpp: a ref built straight from
       this read as a small_real, measured) */
    object_ref self() const { return object_ref{ jank::runtime::detail::untagged(static_cast<object const *>(this)) }; }
    jtl::immutable_string to_string() const override {
      if(printer == jank_nil) return \"#eve/object\";
      return jank::runtime::to_string(printer.call(self()));
    }
    void to_string(jtl::string_builder &sb) const override { sb(to_string()); }
    jtl::immutable_string to_code_string() const override { return to_string(); }
    bool equal(object const &o) const override {
      if(&o == this) return true;
      if(equiv == jank_nil) return false;
      return truthy(equiv.call(self(), object_ref{ jank::runtime::detail::untagged(&o) }));
    }
    jank::uhash to_hash() const override {
      if(hasher == jank_nil) return (jank::uhash)reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(this);
      return (jank::uhash)to_int(hasher.call(self()));
    }
    object_ref get(object_ref key) const override {
      if(lookup == jank_nil) return jank_nil;
      return lookup.call(self(), key, jank_nil);
    }
    object_ref get(object_ref key, object_ref fallback) const override {
      if(lookup == jank_nil) return fallback;
      return lookup.call(self(), key, fallback);
    }
    bool contains(object_ref key) const override {
      if(dispatch == jank_nil) return false;
      return truthy(dispatch.call(op(1), self(), key, jank_nil));
    }
    object_ref seq() const override { return dispatch.call(op(2), self(), jank_nil, jank_nil); }
    object_ref fresh_seq() const override { return seq(); }
    /* a type that is its own seq (eve.core's seq returns it as itself): jank 0.1 walks an object through these
       virtuals whatever its behavior bits (measured: eve/probes/jank-seqlike) — the base's first/next of an object
       whose seq is itself never ended. A type's own ISeq through the hook; any other through its seq. */
    object_ref first() const override { return dispatch.call(op(9), self(), jank_nil, jank_nil); }
    object_ref next() const override { return dispatch.call(op(10), self(), jank_nil, jank_nil); }
    object_ref next_in_place() override { return next(); }
    object_ref nth(object_ref index) const override { return dispatch.call(op(3), self(), index, jank_nil); }
    object_ref nth(object_ref index, object_ref fallback) const override { return dispatch.call(op(4), self(), index, fallback); }
    object_ref call(object_ref const a) const override { return dispatch.call(op(5), self(), a, jank_nil); }
    object_ref call(object_ref const a, object_ref const b) const override { return dispatch.call(op(6), self(), a, b); }
    object_ref find(object_ref key) const override { return dispatch.call(op(7), self(), key, jank_nil); }
    /* compare: the type's own IComparable (identity audit B-COMPARE: jank's compare had no Eve answer to reach) */
    jank::i64 compare(object const &o) const override {
      return to_int(dispatch.call(op(8), self(), object_ref{ jank::runtime::detail::untagged(&o) }, jank_nil));
    }
  };
  object_ref make(object_ref tag, object_ref fields) { return make_box<eve_obj>(tag, fields); }
  bool is(object_ref o) { return o.get_type() == object_type::opaque_box && dynamic_cast<eve_obj *>(o.ptr()) != nullptr; }
  object_ref tag(object_ref o) { return static_cast<eve_obj *>(o.ptr())->tag; }
  object_ref fields(object_ref o) { return static_cast<eve_obj *>(o.ptr())->fields; }
  void set_printer(object_ref f) { root(); printer = f; }
  void set_equiv(object_ref f) { root(); equiv = f; }
  void set_hasher(object_ref f) { root(); hasher = f; }
  void set_lookup(object_ref f) { root(); lookup = f; }
  void set_dispatch(object_ref f) { root(); dispatch = f; }
  /* = of x and y is jank's own equal when neither is an opaque object (an eve instance's type, whose own equivalence
     answers first) and either is a scalar (nil, boolean, number, string, keyword, symbol, character: object_type's
     enumerators through character, but the string sequence): eve='s element walk runs only for two jank maps or two
     sequentials, and its other arms answer false where jank's equal did */
  static bool scalar_type(object_type const t) { return t <= object_type::character && t != object_type::persistent_string_sequence; }
  bool eq_plain(object_ref x, object_ref y) {
    object_type const tx{ x.get_type() }, ty{ y.get_type() };
    return tx != object_type::opaque_box && ty != object_type::opaque_box && (scalar_type(tx) || scalar_type(ty));
  }
  /* A protocol table's key for x in one call: an eve instance's tag; nil's key (::nil); jank's own type name for every
     other value but a map — the name boxed once per object_type at load (jank's type boxed a fresh string per call:
     532 ns a vector's key, measured probe2 P7) — and nil for a map, whose record tag (its meta's :eve/record) the
     Clojure side reads. The table is written once, by init_type_keys at load, and read only after. */
  static object_ref nil_key{ jank_nil };
  static object_ref type_names[static_cast<int>(object_type::max) + 1];
  static bool keys_rooted{ false };
  void init_type_keys(object_ref nk) {
    if(!keys_rooted) {
      keys_rooted = true;
      GC_add_roots(&nil_key, &nil_key + 1);
      GC_add_roots(&type_names[0], &type_names[0] + (static_cast<int>(object_type::max) + 1));
    }
    nil_key = nk;
    for(int i = 0; i <= static_cast<int>(object_type::max); ++i) {
      type_names[i] = make_box(object_type_str(static_cast<object_type>(i)));
    }
  }
  object_ref type_key(object_ref x) {
    object_type const t{ x.get_type() };
    if(t == object_type::nil) return nil_key;
    if(t == object_type::opaque_box) {
      if(auto const *e = dynamic_cast<eve_obj *>(x.ptr())) return e->tag;
      return type_names[static_cast<int>(t)];
    }
    if(is_map(x)) return jank_nil;
    return type_names[static_cast<int>(t)];
  }
  /* every entry of publics (a map of symbol to var) referred into namespace cur: the per-var refer jank's refer makes,
     in one C++ loop (ns.hpp has no bulk refer) */
  object_ref refer_all(object_ref cur, object_ref publics) {
    for(object_ref it{ jank::runtime::seq(publics) }; !it.is_nil(); it = jank::runtime::next(it)) {
      object_ref const e{ jank::runtime::first(it) };
      jank::runtime::refer(cur, jank::runtime::first(e), jank::runtime::second(e));
    }
    return jank_nil;
  }
  long addr(object_ref o) { return (long)reinterpret_cast<uintptr_t>(o.ptr()); }
  long now_millis() { return (long)std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::milliseconds>(std::chrono::system_clock::now().time_since_epoch()).count(); }
  /* a byte array of eve's is signed (HOST-CONTRACT §3: a byte reads back signed, as the JVM's): jank's own
     byte-array is u8, so eve's are obj::array<i8> made here */
  object_ref i8_array(long n) { return make_box<obj::array<jank::i8>>((jank::i64)n); }
}
")

(defn make-object
  "An instance of the deftype whose tag is tag (a symbol), over fields (a vector: a mutable field's cell among them)."
  [tag fields]
  (cpp/eve_host.make tag fields))

(defn object?
  "x is a deftype or reify instance."
  [x]
  (cpp/eve_host.is x))

(defn object-tag [x] (cpp/eve_host.tag x))
(defn object-fields [x] (cpp/eve_host.fields x))
(defn object-addr "The instance's address (identity-hash)." [x] (cpp/eve_host.addr x))

(def type-fields
  "Every deftype's field names by tag, in order (its factory's argument order): what a field read by name looks up."
  (atom {}))

(def type-mutable
  "Every deftype's mutable field names by tag (a set): the fields whose slot holds a cell (volatile!) its factory
   made. get-field derefs those only — an immutable field whose VALUE is a volatile (eve.host's (token), an
   eve.rrb-vector transient's ^:host edit token) reads as itself, not as the cell's contents (F-3 family: tally's
   rrb row threw \"conj! after persistent!\" when the edit token read nil)."
  (atom {}))

(def type-field-index
  "Every deftype's fields by tag, each name to [its index, whether it is mutable] — type-fields and type-mutable
   folded into one map, written beside them at deftype time: a field read by name is one get here (it was a
   keep-indexed walk of type-fields with = per name and a second atom's set: 3,791 ns a read, measured
   /home/user/stage/probes/probe2.jank P4)."
  (atom {}))

(defn field-entries
  "names (a type's fields in order) and cs (its mutable ones, a set) as type-field-index holds them."
  [names cs]
  (into {} (map-indexed (fn [i f] [f [i (contains? cs f)]]) names)))

(defn field-index
  "The index of field f (a symbol) in the type tagged tag; nil for none."
  [tag f]
  (when-let [e (get (get (cpp/jank.runtime.deref type-field-index) tag) f)] (nth e 0)))

(defn get-field
  "The value of field f (a symbol) of a deftype instance x — a mutable field's cell's value — as (.-f x) reads it
   where a host's analyzer can; a record's by its key; nil for a field x does not have."
  [x f]
  (cond (cpp/eve_host.is x) (when-let [e (get (get (cpp/jank.runtime.deref type-field-index) (cpp/eve_host.tag x)) f)]
                              (let [v (nth (cpp/eve_host.fields x) (nth e 0))]
                                (if (nth e 1) (cpp/jank.runtime.deref v) v)))
        (map? x) (get x (keyword (name f)))
        :else nil))

(defn set-field!
  "Sets mutable field f (a symbol) of deftype instance x to v, as (set! (.-f x) v) does where a host's analyzer can see
   x's type: the field's cell is reset. v; an ex-info for a field x does not hold mutable."
  [x f v]
  (let [tag (when (object? x) (object-tag x))
        e (when tag (get (get (cpp/jank.runtime.deref type-field-index) tag) f))]
    (if (and e (nth e 1))
      (do (vreset! (nth (object-fields x) (nth e 0)) v) v)
      (throw (ex-info "set! of a field that is not a mutable field of this object" {:field f :type tag})))))

(defn record?*
  "x is a defrecord instance (a map with :eve/record in its meta); jank's core has no record?."
  [x]
  (and (map? x) (some? (:eve/record (meta x)))))

(def ^:private core-type type)

(cpp/eve_host.init_type_keys ::nil)

(defn type-key
  "What a protocol table is keyed by: a deftype's tag, a record's, ::nil for nil, else jank's own type name (a string)."
  [x]
  (let [k (cpp/eve_host.type_key x)]
    (if (nil? k) (or (:eve/record (meta x)) (core-type x)) k)))

(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/type (fn [_] (fn [x] (when (some? x) (type-key x)))))
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/class (fn [_] (fn [x] (when (some? x) (type-key x)))))

(defn- type-of-name
  "The table key a type names in extend-type / instance?: a deftype's var holds its tag; Object, java.lang.Object
   and default are every value; nil is nil; a string names one of jank's own types; another symbol names one by
   its name."
  [t]
  (cond (nil? t) ::nil
        (contains? '#{Object java.lang.Object default} t) ::default
        (= :default t) ::default
        (string? t) t
        ;; a deftype's tag is qualified; an unqualified symbol names one of jank's own types, as type answers it
        (symbol? t) (if (namespace t) t (name t))
        (keyword? t) t
        :else t))

(declare extends?)

(require 'clojure.string)

(defn- class-simple-name
  "The simple name of a class name as written: clojure.lang.Seqable → \"Seqable\", Iterable →
   \"Iterable\". On this seat a dotted symbol is ONE name — (namespace 'clojure.lang.Seqable) is
   nil and (name ...) is the whole dotted string (measured: probe D2, ds-collate lane) — while
   clj-class-protos is keyed by simple names, so a (name t) lookup of a dotted class symbol
   never hits. The segment after the last dot is the simple name on every seat."
  [t]
  (last (clojure.string/split (name t) #"\.")))

(def ^:private clj-class-protos
  "A JVM interface name (its simple name) → the eve.core protocol that answers instance? for it:
   vanilla :clj code tests (instance? clojure.lang.Seqable x) and its kin, where the class is a
   protocol question about the value's own type."
  {"Seqable" 'ISeqable "Associative" 'IAssociative "ILookup" 'ILookup "Indexed" 'IIndexed
   "IPersistentMap" 'IMap "IPersistentVector" 'IVector "IPersistentSet" 'ISet
   "IPersistentCollection" 'ICollection "IFn" 'IFn "Counted" 'ICounted "ISeq" 'ISeq
   "IPersistentList" 'IList "Map" 'IMap "List" 'IVector "Collection" 'ICollection
   "Iterable" 'ISeqable "Sequential" 'ISequential})

(def ^:private clj-host-protos
  "A JVM interface name (its simple name) -> the completion's own protocol that answers
   instance? for it: the atom-family interfaces have no eve.core protocol - the types
   adapter puts them on the completion's protocols (its completion-interfaces table),
   so instance? answers from the completion's own registry, by the value's tag
   (F-JANK-INSTANCE-HOST-PROTOS: datascript.conn/conn? tests clojure.lang.IDeref,
   which fell to the type-key comparison and answered false for a Conn)."
  {"IDeref" 'IDeref "IBlockingDeref" 'IBlockingDeref "IAtom" 'IAtom
   "IAtom2" 'IAtom2 "IPending" 'IPending})

(defn clj-comparable?
  "instance? Comparable on this seat: the scalar kinds the seat's compare orders natively.
   Any other value answers false, as a JVM class without Comparable does in the port's
   value-compare dispatch (the caller falls through to class-compare)."
  [x]
  (or (number? x) (string? x) (keyword? x) (symbol? x) (char? x) (true? x) (false? x)))

(defn clj-bigint? [x] (= "big_integer" (type-key x)))
(defn clj-nan? [x] (not= x x))
(defn clj-ratio? [x] (= "ratio" (type-key x)))
(defn clj-bigdecimal? [_] false)

(def ^:private clj-class-preds
  "A JVM class name (its simple name) that is a predicate question on this seat rather than a
   protocol: (instance? Number x) is number?; (instance? Comparable x) is clj-comparable?.
   Consulted alongside clj-class-protos by clj-instance? and the instance? re-root."
  {"Number" clojure.core/number? "Comparable" clj-comparable?
   "BigInteger" clj-bigint? "BigInt" clj-bigint?
   "Ratio" clj-ratio? "BigDecimal" clj-bigdecimal?
   ;; the scalar-leaf screen of eve.atom's swap! dispatch (ds11-jvm-reads FIX, atom.cljc scalar-leaf?): its :clj
   ;; arm — the one jank's reader takes — tests (instance? String v) and its kin; a JVM class name is no value on
   ;; this seat (measured 2026-11-09, compiled-jank lane: "The symbol `String` could not be resolved" loading
   ;; eve.atom), so clj-face rewrites each to the seat's predicate through this table
   "String" clojure.core/string? "Boolean" clojure.core/boolean? "Character" clojure.core/char?
   "Keyword" clojure.core/keyword? "Symbol" clojure.core/symbol?
   "Date" clojure.core/inst? "UUID" clojure.core/uuid?})


(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/instance?
  (fn [_]
    (fn [t x]
      (let [k (type-of-name t)]
        (cond (= ::default k) (some? x)
              (= ::nil k) (nil? x)
              ;; a JVM interface name: the value's own type extending the protocol, as
              ;; eve-predicate resolves one (eve.core may not be loaded: then nothing extends it)
              (and (symbol? t) (contains? clj-class-preds (class-simple-name t)))
              ((get clj-class-preds (class-simple-name t)) x)
              (and (symbol? t) (contains? clj-host-protos (class-simple-name t)))
              (and (some? x)
                   (extends? @(ns-resolve 'eve.host-completion (get clj-host-protos (class-simple-name t))) (object-tag x)))
              (and (symbol? t) (contains? clj-class-protos (class-simple-name t)))
              (and (some? x) (some? (find-ns 'eve.core))
                   (extends? @(ns-resolve 'eve.core (get clj-class-protos (class-simple-name t))) (type-key x)))
              :else (and (some? x) (= k (type-key x))))))))

;; with-meta on a defrecord instance: a record here is a map whose TYPE lives in
;; its meta (:eve/record - defrecord's constructors), so replacing the meta
;; wholesale strips the type and every protocol the record answers (measured:
;; datascript.parser's with-source on a parsed Pattern - the record kept its
;; fields but satisfied nothing, collect-vars read none of its vars, and query
;; validation raised "unknown vars"). On the JVM with-meta never changes an
;; object's type; keep the marker (F-JANK-WITH-META-RECORD).
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/with-meta
  (fn [orig]
    (fn [x m]
      (if-let [r (when (map? x) (:eve/record (meta x)))]
        (orig x (assoc m :eve/record r))
        (orig x m)))))

(defn util-hash-combine
  "clojure.lang.Util/hashCombine — the JVM's int hash mixer, named as a static call by vanilla
   :clj code (datascript.db's combine-hashes): x ^ (y + 0x9e3779b9 + (x << 6) + (x >>> 2)),
   computed in int arithmetic (each step wrapped to 32 bits, as the JVM's int ops wrap)."
  [x y]
  (let [x (int x) y (int y)]
    (int (bit-xor x
                  (int (+ y 2654435769
                          (int (bit-shift-left x 6))
                          (int (bit-shift-right (bit-and x 0xffffffff) 2))))))))

(defn clj-instance?
  "instance? against a JVM interface name (the symbol as written: clojure.lang.Seqable, java.util.Map,
   Iterable): the value's own type extending the eve.core protocol clj-class-protos names. A class
   symbol never resolves as a value here (jank's analyzer reads clojure.lang.<Name> as a class, and
   there is no class), so clj-face rewrites the (instance? <name> x) form to this call."
  [t x]
  (if (contains? clj-class-preds (class-simple-name t))
    ((get clj-class-preds (class-simple-name t)) x)
    (if (contains? clj-host-protos (class-simple-name t))
      (and (some? x)
           (extends? @(ns-resolve 'eve.host-completion (get clj-host-protos (class-simple-name t))) (object-tag x)))
      (and (some? x) (some? (find-ns 'eve.core))
           (extends? @(ns-resolve 'eve.core (get clj-class-protos (class-simple-name t))) (type-key x))))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; +' -' *' exact — jank's promoting_sub wraps at the i64 boundary
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The primed ops are the contract's promoting half, and jank's own promoting_sub breaks it for genuine i64
;; integer operands: measured on this seat (eve.overflow-test, primed-promotes) (-' MIN 1) answered
;; 9223372036854775807N — the i64-wrapped value in a big box — and (-' MIN) answered MIN in a big box, where
;; +' of the same operands answered exactly. promoting_add and promoting_mul share the code shape, so all
;; three are bound here, not just the measured one: for two i64 integers the builtin computes the value; on
;; overflow the exact value is built as a big integer from the operands (eve_arith.as_big, the divide block
;; above). Any other operands keep jank's promoting op. An upstream observation with this repro belongs to
;; jank's tracker; nothing here patches jank.
(cpp/raw "
namespace eve_arith {
  using namespace jank::runtime;
  object_ref exact_add(object_ref const l, object_ref const r) {
    if(i64_integer(l.get_type()) && i64_integer(r.get_type())) {
      jank::i64 res;
      if(__builtin_add_overflow(to_int(l), to_int(r), &res)) {
        return make_box<obj::big_integer>(as_big(l) + as_big(r));
      }
      return make_box(res);
    }
    return promoting_add(l, r);
  }
  object_ref exact_sub(object_ref const l, object_ref const r) {
    if(i64_integer(l.get_type()) && i64_integer(r.get_type())) {
      jank::i64 res;
      if(__builtin_sub_overflow(to_int(l), to_int(r), &res)) {
        return make_box<obj::big_integer>(as_big(l) - as_big(r));
      }
      return make_box(res);
    }
    return promoting_sub(l, r);
  }
  object_ref exact_mul(object_ref const l, object_ref const r) {
    if(i64_integer(l.get_type()) && i64_integer(r.get_type())) {
      jank::i64 res;
      if(__builtin_mul_overflow(to_int(l), to_int(r), &res)) {
        return make_box<obj::big_integer>(as_big(l) * as_big(r));
      }
      return make_box(res);
    }
    return promoting_mul(l, r);
  }
  object_ref exact_negate(object_ref const x) {
    if(i64_integer(x.get_type())) {
      jank::i64 res;
      if(__builtin_sub_overflow(static_cast<jank::i64>(0), to_int(x), &res)) {
        return make_box<obj::big_integer>(-as_big(x));
      }
      return make_box(res);
    }
    return promoting_sub(make_box(static_cast<jank::i64>(0)), x);
  }
}
")

(defn exact-add [l r] (cpp/eve_arith.exact_add l r))
(defn exact-sub [l r] (cpp/eve_arith.exact_sub l r))
(defn exact-mul [l r] (cpp/eve_arith.exact_mul l r))
(defn exact-negate [x] (cpp/eve_arith.exact_negate x))

;; The primed vars are re-rooted only, no :inline: a 2-arity :inline on -' is applied by jank's analyzer to
;; its 1-arity call too (this file's own unchecked-negate calls (-' a)), and the module refuses to load
;; ("Invalid call to fn with 1 args provided": measured). The var root carries the binding — a compiled
;; call answers through it, as the landing lane's probe shows (+' and -' exact at both boundaries).
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/+'
  (fn [_] (fn ([] 0)
              ([x] x)
              ([x y] (exact-add x y))
              ([x y z] (exact-add (exact-add x y) z))
              ([x y z w] (exact-add (exact-add (exact-add x y) z) w))
              ([x y z w & more] (reduce exact-add (exact-add (exact-add (exact-add x y) z) w) more)))))
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/-'
  (fn [_] (fn ([x] (exact-negate x))
              ([x y] (exact-sub x y))
              ([x y z] (exact-sub (exact-sub x y) z))
              ([x y z w] (exact-sub (exact-sub (exact-sub x y) z) w))
              ([x y z w & more] (reduce exact-sub (exact-sub (exact-sub (exact-sub x y) z) w) more)))))
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/*'
  (fn [_] (fn ([] 1)
              ([x] x)
              ([x y] (exact-mul x y))
              ([x y z] (exact-mul (exact-mul x y) z))
              ([x y z w] (exact-mul (exact-mul (exact-mul x y) z) w))
              ([x y z w & more] (reduce exact-mul (exact-mul (exact-mul (exact-mul x y) z) w) more)))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The fixed-width ops jank's core leaves as TODO
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defn- wrap [bits]
  (let [m (dec (bit-shift-left 1 bits)) half (bit-shift-left 1 (dec bits)) full (bit-shift-left 1 bits)]
    (fn [x] (let [u (bit-and (long x) m)] (if (>= u half) (- u full) u)))))

(def ^:private i8 (wrap 8))
(def ^:private i16 (wrap 16))
(def ^:private i32 (wrap 32))

(defn- re-root! [sym f] (alter-var-root (ns-resolve 'clojure.core sym) (fn [_] f)))

;; + - * are checked now (the section at the top of this file), so the unchecked ops are built on the promoting
;; ops +' -' *' and wrap64: a promoting answer past i64 (a big integer) wraps to its low 64 bits, signed, as the
;; JVM's unchecked ops answer. wrap64 goes through mod, never (long <big>): what jank's long cast of a big
;; integer does is not the JVM's BigInteger.longValue contract this needs.
(defn- wrap64 [r]
  (if (cpp/eve_arith.is_big r)
    (let [u (mod r 18446744073709551616)]
      (if (>= u 9223372036854775808) (- u 18446744073709551616) u))
    r))

(re-root! 'unchecked-byte i8)
(re-root! 'unchecked-short i16)
(re-root! 'unchecked-int i32)
(re-root! 'unchecked-long (fn [x] (if (cpp/eve_arith.is_big x) (wrap64 x) (long x))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-add (fn [a b] (wrap64 (+' a b))))

;; Eduction: jank's clojure.core has no Eduction type, factory or fn (probed: ->Eduction,
;; Eduction and eduction all unresolvable). Libraries call ->Eduction in deftype method bodies
;; (datascript's -search wraps index slices in it). The seat's eduction is the reducible seq
;; view (sequence xform coll): reducible and seqable, which is how the results are consumed.
(intern 'clojure.core '->Eduction (fn [xform coll] (sequence xform coll)))
(intern 'clojure.core 'eduction
        (fn ([xform coll] (sequence xform coll))
            ([xform coll & xforms] (sequence (apply comp xform xforms) coll))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-subtract (fn [a b] (wrap64 (-' a b))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-multiply (fn [a b] (wrap64 (*' a b))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-inc (fn [a] (wrap64 (+' a 1))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-dec (fn [a] (wrap64 (-' a 1))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-negate (fn [a] (wrap64 (-' a))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-add-int (fn [a b] (i32 (wrap64 (+' a b)))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-subtract-int (fn [a b] (i32 (wrap64 (-' a b)))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-multiply-int (fn [a b] (i32 (*' (i32 a) (i32 b)))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-inc-int (fn [a] (i32 (wrap64 (+' a 1)))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-dec-int (fn [a] (i32 (wrap64 (-' a 1)))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-negate-int (fn [a] (i32 (wrap64 (-' a)))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-divide-int (fn [a b] (i32 (quot a b))))
(re-root! 'unchecked-remainder-int (fn [a b] (i32 (rem a b))))
(re-root! 'byte i8)
(re-root! 'short i16)
(re-root! 'cast (fn [_ x] x))

;; aset-byte, aset-short, aset-int, aset-long, aset-float, aset-double, aset-boolean: jank's core generates each as
;; (throw "TODO: port …") — a throw of a string literal, which is a C++ throw of a char const* that no jank catch takes,
;; so the process ends ("terminate called after throwing an instance of 'char const*'", exit 134: eve.reference-tag-test
;; at a-foreign-or-unknown-reference-is-refused, its with-byte helper — the F-4 abort; eve/probes/jank-bytes). Each
;; sets through jank's aset, the value coerced to the array's width, and answers it, as Clojure's do.
(doseq [[sym coerce] [['aset-byte i8] ['aset-short i16] ['aset-int i32] ['aset-long (fn [x] (long x))]
                      ['aset-float (fn [x] (double x))] ['aset-double (fn [x] (double x))]
                      ['aset-boolean (fn [x] (boolean x))]]]
  (re-root! sym (fn ([a i v] (let [v (coerce v)] (clojure.core/aset a i v) v))
                    ([a i j & more] (apply (ns-resolve 'clojure.core sym) (clojure.core/aget a i) j more)))))

;; eve's byte arrays are signed (a byte reads back -128..127, as the JVM's: HOST-CONTRACT §3, the slab-io conformance's
;; rows): jank's byte-array makes u8 arrays, so it is re-rooted to i8 arrays (its inline dropped first)
(defn- i8-array
  ([n] (if (number? n)
         (cpp/eve_host.i8_array (long n))
         (let [xs (vec n) a (cpp/eve_host.i8_array (long (count xs)))]
           (dotimes [i (count xs)] (clojure.core/aset a i (i8 (nth xs i))))
           a)))
  ([n init] (let [a (cpp/eve_host.i8_array (long n))] (dotimes [i n] (clojure.core/aset a i (i8 init))) a)))
(alter-meta! #'clojure.core/byte-array dissoc :inline :inline-arities)
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/byte-array (fn [_] i8-array))

;; the casts int, long, double, float, short, byte and char are inlined to native C++ values, which jank's codegen
;; cannot box as a fn's result or a case's value ((count [_] (int cnt)) in a type: "no viable overloaded '=' … int to
;; oref", measured on eve.array's type); called as functions they answer boxed, so their inline expansions are dropped
(doseq [sym '[int long double float short byte char]]
  (alter-meta! (ns-resolve 'clojure.core sym) dissoc :inline :inline-arities))

;; object-array's inline expansion types its result, and jank's inline aset on a typed object array is an ambiguous
;; C++ overload (array_ref<object_ref> with a T and an object_ref value both object_ref: measured, a compile error at
;; the call site); called as a function, the array reaches aset untyped and the runtime overload answers.
(alter-meta! #'clojure.core/object-array dissoc :inline :inline-arities)

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Type hints: dropped from every binding, so no value is a C++ native and no hint is a C++ type
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; jank reads ^long on a parameter or a let/loop local as a native C++ long, and its case* codegen cannot box one
;; that reaches a case form's dispatch or a branch ("no viable overloaded '=' … long to oref", core.jank:4523:
;; measured, `(defn f [^long h] (case h 1 :one h))`); and a hint naming an eve type, as eve.deftype-proto.sio's
;; `(defn T-offset [^T inst] ...)` does, is "Parameter type meta data is expected to be a symbol or list which
;; resolves to a C++ type … a `var_unbound_root` instead" (measured, eve.dataset's Dataset). eve's shared code hints
;; ^long in 78 places (the JVM's primitive hint) and its types by name, so defn, defn-, fn, let and loop are re-rooted
;; here to drop the :tag from every binding symbol before the core macro expands: every value stays boxed on jank (the
;; cpp/raw aliases above cover the hints the strip does not reach, a deftype method's parameters among them). jank's
;; reader stores a hint as :tag (quote long), not the symbol (measured).

(defn- tag-of [x]
  (let [t (:tag (meta x))] (if (and (seq? t) (= 'quote (first t))) (second t) t)))

(defn- untag-native
  "x with its :tag dropped (every hint: a native's, an eve type's, a JVM class's — none is a C++ type eve means)."
  [x]
  (if (and (symbol? x) (some? (tag-of x))) (vary-meta x dissoc :tag) x))

(defn- strip-bindings
  "A binding form or arglist with the native tags dropped from its symbols (through vectors and destructuring maps)."
  [form]
  (cond (symbol? form) (untag-native form)
        (vector? form) (with-meta (mapv strip-bindings form) (dissoc (meta form) :tag))
        (map? form) (with-meta (into {} (map (fn [kv] [(strip-bindings (key kv)) (val kv)]) form)) (meta form))
        :else form))

(defn- strip-fn-tail
  "A fn's tail — name? docstring? attr-map? then [params] body, or ([params] body)... — with its arglists stripped."
  [tail]
  (map (fn [x] (cond (vector? x) (strip-bindings x)
                     (and (sequential? x) (not (vector? x)) (vector? (first x))) (cons (strip-bindings (first x)) (rest x))
                     :else x))
       tail))

;; jank's fixed-arity limit is 10 parameters ("This function has too many parameters. The max is 10": upstream defect
;; 13); eve.deftype-proto.sio's ->T constructor takes one per field and one more with a leading sio (IntMapBranch has
;; 19). A fn with an arity past the limit becomes one variadic arity dispatching on its argument count to each arity's
;; body under a let of its parameters (a variadic arity the default; none, an ex-info).
(defn- arity? [x] (and (sequential? x) (not (vector? x)) (vector? (first x))))

(defn- wide-arities
  "A fn tail (after the name) whose arities all take at most 10 parameters is itself; past that, the tail with one
   variadic arity dispatching on the count of its arguments."
  [tail]
  (let [[pre body] (split-with #(not (or (vector? %) (arity? %))) tail)
        arities (if (vector? (first body)) [body] body)
        n-fixed (fn [params] (count (take-while #(not= '& %) params)))
        variadic? (fn [[params]] (some #(= '& %) params))]
    (if-not (some (fn [[params]] (> (n-fixed params) 10)) arities)
      tail
      (let [args (gensym "args")
            clauses (mapcat (fn [[params & b]] [(count params) (list* 'clojure.core/let [params args] b)])
                            (remove variadic? arities))
            default (if-let [[params & b] (first (filter variadic? arities))]
                      (list* 'clojure.core/let [params args] b)
                      (list 'throw (list 'ex-info "wrong number of arguments" {:count (list 'clojure.core/count args)})))]
        (concat pre [(list ['& args]
                           (list* 'clojure.core/case (list 'clojure.core/count args) (concat clauses [default])))])))))

;; A field read written (.-f x) — stock Clojure, and every external .cljc structure's — on a target whose type jank's
;; analyzer cannot see compiles to a C++ member access on an object_ref, which cannot exist ("There is no `edit`
;; member within jank::runtime::oref<jank::runtime::object>": Lane M's identity audit B-RRB, 148 sites on the release
;; tree). Such a read can never have compiled on jank, so the bodies defn, defn-, fn, let and loop expand are walked
;; first and each (.-f x) becomes the completion's field read (get-field: a deftype's field by name, a record's by
;; key) — the field is the Eve object's, whatever the analyzer sees (the operator's analyzer-deferral route). It
;; covers a read of another instance through an untyped parameter as well as this one's (`(.-keys next)` in a Node
;; method: Lane M's external case, probes/jank-deferral), the other spelling (. x -f), and a write, (set! (.-f x) v)
;; or (set! (. x -f) v), which becomes set-field! (the mutable field's cell reset). Quoted forms are left as they are.
(defn- field-read-sym [s]
  (when (and (symbol? s) (nil? (namespace s)))
    (let [n (name s)] (when (and (> (count n) 2) (= ".-" (subs n 0 2))) (symbol (subs n 2))))))

(defn- dot-field-sym
  "f of (. x -f), the other spelling of a field read; nil for any other (. x ...)."
  [form]
  (when (and (= '. (first form)) (= 3 (count form)) (symbol? (nth form 2)) (nil? (namespace (nth form 2))))
    (let [n (name (nth form 2))] (when (and (> (count n) 1) (= "-" (subs n 0 1))) (symbol (subs n 1))))))

(defn- defer-field-reads [form]
  (cond (seq? form)
        (let [h (first form) f (field-read-sym h)
              target (when (and (= 'set! h) (= 3 (count form)) (seq? (second form))) (second form))
              tf (when target (or (and (= 2 (count target)) (field-read-sym (first target))) (dot-field-sym target)))]
          (cond (= 'quote h) form
                (and f (= 2 (count form))) (list 'eve.host-completion/get-field (defer-field-reads (second form))
                                                 (list 'quote f))
                (dot-field-sym form) (list 'eve.host-completion/get-field (defer-field-reads (second form))
                                           (list 'quote (dot-field-sym form)))
                ;; a write, (set! (.-f x) v) or (set! (. x -f) v): the object's cell
                tf (list 'eve.host-completion/set-field! (defer-field-reads (second target)) (list 'quote tf)
                         (defer-field-reads (nth form 2)))
                :else (with-meta (apply list (map defer-field-reads form)) (meta form))))
        (vector? form) (with-meta (mapv defer-field-reads form) (meta form))
        (map? form) (with-meta (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(defer-field-reads k) (defer-field-reads v)])) form) (meta form))
        :else form))

(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/defn
  (fn [core] (fn [form env name & tail]
               (apply core form env (untag-native name) (wide-arities (strip-fn-tail (map defer-field-reads tail)))))))
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/defn-
  (fn [core] (fn [form env name & tail]
               (apply core form env (untag-native name) (wide-arities (strip-fn-tail (map defer-field-reads tail)))))))
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/fn
  (fn [core] (fn [form env & tail] (apply core form env (wide-arities (strip-fn-tail (map defer-field-reads tail)))))))
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/let
  (fn [core] (fn [form env bindings & body]
               (apply core form env (if (vector? bindings) (strip-bindings (defer-field-reads bindings)) bindings)
                      (map defer-field-reads body)))))
;; A loop local whose init is an integer literal keeps the literal's C++ int width through recur (upstream defect
;; 21): (loop [p 1 i 0] (if (< i 32) (recur (* p 2) (inc i)) p)) answers 0, with + - * exact above. Such an init
;; is boxed here — (clojure.core/identity 1) — so the local is an object and holds what recur gives it (measured:
;; 4294967296; eve/probes/jank-xxh3/probe4.cljc). eve.hamt-util's pow2 table is such a loop (rows 31 and 32 read
;; -2147483648 and 0 without it), and dotimes's counter.
;; A boolean or char literal init likewise makes a native local, which a recur of a value that is nil at run time
;; cannot take: "An object of type `boolean` was expected here, but a `nil` was provided instead" (Clojure's boolean
;; and char loop locals are objects: legal there) — eve.thread.domain's loops (eve.thread-domain-test's 3 errors,
;; eve.thread-fold-group-test's fold-on-a-group); measured: eve/probes/jank-loop/probe-bool.jank.
(defn- box-int-inits
  "A loop's binding vector with each integer, boolean or char literal init wrapped in identity."
  [bindings]
  (with-meta (vec (mapcat (fn [[b init]] [b (if (or (integer? init) (boolean? init) (char? init))
                                               (list 'clojure.core/identity init)
                                               init)])
                          (partition 2 bindings)))
             (meta bindings)))

;; A loop nested in a loop that rebinds the outer one's locals fails jank's C++ codegen (upstream defect 24: "use of
;; undeclared identifier 's47'"; measured with eve.rrb-vector.rrbt's Vector -nth shape: eve/probes/jank-loop), which
;; ended tally's rrb row and eve.net.bignum's redc (the crypto fast path) once their deferred fns compiled. So every
;; loop is written as Clojure's own loop writes a destructuring one: its bindings, in order, in a let (each init
;; bound to a fresh name, the target to that name — sequential, as loop's are), loop* over the fresh names, the
;; targets bound again inside. No two loops then share a local's name; recur still rebinds the loop's own locals.
(defn- fresh-loop
  "A loop's [bindings body] as [let-bindings loop-bindings inner-let-bindings] over fresh names."
  [bindings]
  (let [pairs (partition 2 bindings)
        gs (mapv (fn [[b _]] (gensym (str (if (symbol? b) (name b) "b") "__loop"))) pairs)]
    [(vec (mapcat (fn [g [b init]] [g init b g]) gs pairs))
     (vec (mapcat (fn [g] [g g]) gs))
     (vec (mapcat (fn [g [b _]] [b g]) gs pairs))]))

(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/loop
  (fn [core] (fn [form env bindings & body]
               (let [bindings (defer-field-reads bindings) body (map defer-field-reads body)]
               (if (and (vector? bindings) (seq bindings))
                 (let [[outer lp inner] (fresh-loop (box-int-inits (strip-bindings bindings)))]
                   (list 'clojure.core/let outer
                         (apply core form env lp (list (list* 'clojure.core/let inner body)))))
                 (apply core form env (if (vector? bindings) (strip-bindings bindings) bindings) body))))))

;; jank's defmacro expands to `(reset-meta! (var name) (assoc (meta (var name)) :macro true))` with meta and assoc
;; unqualified, so a namespace that excludes meta from clojure.core (eve.alpha, which refers eve.core's) cannot define a
;; macro: "The symbol `meta` could not be resolved" (measured; upstream defect 20). Re-rooted to qualify them.
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/defmacro
  (fn [core]
    (fn [form env name & tail]
      (let [[do-sym defn-form _ var-form] (apply core form env name tail)]
        (list do-sym defn-form
              (list 'clojure.core/reset-meta! var-form
                    (list 'clojure.core/assoc (list 'clojure.core/meta var-form) :macro true))
              var-form)))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; case: the default clause boxed
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; jank's case* stores its result in an object_ref and assigns each branch's value to it boxed, but not the default
;; clause's: a default C++-typed natively fails to compile ("no viable overloaded '=' … bool to oref", core.jank:4523
;; for integer constants, 4531 for keywords, 4527 for strings and symbols) — a literal true/false, integer, double or
;; string (const char*), a let ending in one, an if of literals, (boolean x) (measured, 25 shapes,
;; probes/jank-case/out1..4.txt: `(defn f [x] (case x 1 true false))` fails; `(case x 1 false 2 true :d)` and
;; `(case x 1 :a (clojure.core/identity false))` answer). eve.set's hamt-find ends `(case (int nt) 1 … 2 … false)`, so
;; an Eve set's first walk (two sets holding a by-reference member, whose digests abstain) died at its deferred
;; compile. So every case's default is passed through clojure.core/identity (an object) — keyword, string and symbol
;; cases stay jank's own hashed dispatch (they compile once the default is boxed: measured; the cond route this
;; replaced worked around the same defect). A default holding a recur is left as it is: identity would take the recur
;; out of tail position, and an if over a recur and a literal compiles (measured). (Upstream defect 19, amended.)

(defn- has-recur? [form]
  (cond (= 'recur form) true
        (or (seq? form) (vector? form)) (boolean (some has-recur? form))
        (map? form) (boolean (some has-recur? (concat (keys form) (vals form))))
        :else false))

(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/case
  (fn [core]
    (fn [form env e & clauses]
      (if (odd? (count clauses))
        (let [d (last clauses)]
          (apply core form env e (concat (butlast clauses)
                                         [(if (has-recur? d) d (list 'clojure.core/identity d))])))
        (apply core form env e clauses)))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Protocols: a table per method keyed by type key; a method fn of fixed arities caching its impl
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defn impl-for
  "The fn protocol p's method k is for x: the impl extended to x's type key, else to nil (x nil), else the default
   (Object) one — cached in cache (a volatile map) under the key."
  [p k x cache]
  (let [m @p
        tk (type-key x)
        fns (:fns m)
        f (or (get-in fns [tk k])
              (when (some? x) (get-in fns [::default k])))]
    (when-not f
      (throw (ex-info (str "No implementation of method: " (name k) " of protocol: " (:name m)
                           " found for type: " (if (nil? x) "nil" (str tk)))
                      {:protocol (:name m) :method k :type tk})))
    (vswap! cache assoc tk f)
    f))

(defmacro defprotocol
  "A protocol: an atom {:name :sigs :fns {type-key {method fn}} :impls [type-keys] :caches [..]} and one fn per
   method, of the arities its signature lists, dispatching on its first argument's type key."
  [pname & opts+sigs]
  (let [sigs (filter seq? opts+sigs)]
    `(do (def ~pname (atom {:name '~(symbol (str *ns*) (name pname))
                            :sigs '~sigs :impls [] :fns {} :caches []}))
         ~@(for [[mname & specs] sigs
                 :let [cache (gensym "cache")
                       arglists (filter vector? specs)]]
             `(let [~cache (volatile! {})]
                (swap! ~pname update :caches conj ~cache)
                (def ~mname
                  (fn ~@(for [al arglists
                              :let [as (vec (repeatedly (count al) #(gensym "a")))]]
                          `(~as ((or (get (cpp/jank.runtime.deref ~cache) (eve.host-completion/type-key ~(first as)))
                                     (eve.host-completion/impl-for ~pname ~(keyword (name mname)) ~(first as) ~cache))
                                 ~@as)))))))
         (var ~pname))))

(defn extend
  "(extend type-name proto mmap proto mmap ...): mmap's fns (keyword method names) become proto's for the type."
  [atype & proto+mmaps]
  (let [k (type-of-name atype)]
    (doseq [[p mmap] (partition 2 proto+mmaps)]
      (swap! p (fn [m] (-> m
                           (update :impls (fn [is] (if (some #(= k %) is) is (conj (vec is) k))))
                           (update-in [:fns k] merge mmap)
                           (dissoc :sat))))
      (doseq [c (:caches @p)] (vreset! c {})))
    nil))

(defn satisfies?
  "true when protocol p has been extended to x's type key, or to every value (Object) and x is not nil."
  [p x]
  (let [k (type-key x)
        m @p
        cached (get (:sat m) k ::none)]
    (if (identical? cached ::none)
      (let [r (boolean (or (contains? (:fns m) k)
                           (and (some? x) (contains? (:fns m) ::default))))]
        (swap! p assoc-in [:sat k] r)
        r)
      cached)))

(defn extends?
  "true when protocol p has been extended to the type named atype itself."
  [p atype]
  (contains? (:fns @p) (type-of-name atype)))

(defn- entry-arities
  "A method entry's arities: (name [args] body...) is one; (name ([args] body...) ...) lists them."
  [e]
  (if (vector? (second e)) [(rest e)] (rest e)))

(defn- method-map
  "Method entries ((name [args] body...) or (name ([args] body...) ...), several entries per name allowed) as
   {:name (fn ([args] body...) ...)}."
  [entries]
  (into {} (for [[nm es] (group-by first entries)]
             [(keyword (name nm))
              (cons 'clojure.core/fn (mapcat entry-arities es))])))

(defn- parse-impls
  "A body of protocol then its methods, as [[protocol [(name [args] body...) ...]] ...]."
  [specs]
  (loop [out [] s specs]
    (if (seq s)
      (let [p0 (first s)
            ;; a dotted class name in spec position (java.util.Comparator in a reify spec) arrives
            ;; qualified by the defining macro's syntax quote (datascript.db/java.util.Comparator):
            ;; the seat's spec tables are keyed by the bare dotted symbol, so strip the qualification
            p (if (and (symbol? p0) (namespace p0) (not= (name p0) (class-simple-name p0)))
                (symbol (name p0))
                p0)
            [ms more] (split-with seq? (rest s))]
        (recur (conj out [p (vec ms)]) more))
      out)))

(defmacro extend-type
  "(extend-type T Proto (m [this ...] body...) ...): each protocol's methods extended to T."
  [t & specs]
  `(eve.host-completion/extend ~(if (symbol? t) (list 'eve.host-completion/quote-or-value t) t)
     ~@(mapcat (fn [[p ms]] [p (method-map ms)]) (parse-impls specs))))

(defmacro quote-or-value
  "A type name in extend-type: a var's value where the symbol resolves to one (a deftype's tag), else the symbol
   itself (a host type named by its name)."
  [s]
  (if (or (nil? s) (contains? '#{Object java.lang.Object default} s))
    (list 'quote s)
    (if (resolve s) s (list 'quote s))))

(defmacro extend-protocol
  "(extend-protocol Proto T1 (m ...) T2 (m ...) ...)."
  [p & specs]
  (let [groups (loop [out [] s specs]
                 (if (seq s)
                   (let [t (first s) [ms more] (split-with seq? (rest s))]
                     (recur (conj out [t (vec ms)]) more))
                   out))]
    `(do ~@(for [[t ms] groups] `(extend-type ~t ~p ~@ms)) nil)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The atom, deref and pending interfaces of a type (as glojure's completion): jank's deref, swap!, reset!,
;; compare-and-set!, swap-vals!, reset-vals! and realized? are plain functions (not inlined: measured) and take
;; jank's own atoms, delays and futures; for a type they call its IDeref / IAtom / IPending below — what eve's types
;; adapter (adapters/types/jank) translates clojure.lang.IDeref, IAtom, IAtom2 and IPending onto.
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defprotocol IDeref (-deref [o]))
(defprotocol IBlockingDeref (-deref-within [o ms timeout-val]))
(defprotocol IAtom
  (-swap [a f] [a f x] [a f x y] [a f x y more])
  (-reset [a v])
  (-compare-and-set [a old new]))
(defprotocol IAtom2
  (-swap-vals [a f] [a f x] [a f x y] [a f x y more])
  (-reset-vals [a v]))
(defprotocol IPending (-realized? [o]))

(defn- host-ref?
  "x is one of jank's own (its atom, delay, volatile, var ...): not a type's instance."
  [x]
  (not (object? x)))

(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/deref
  (fn [core]
    (fn ([x] (if (host-ref? x) (core x) (-deref x)))
      ([x ms timeout-val]
       (if (host-ref? x) (core x ms timeout-val) (-deref-within x ms timeout-val))))))

(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/swap!
  (fn [core]
    (fn ([a f] (if (host-ref? a) (core a f) (-swap a f)))
      ([a f x] (if (host-ref? a) (core a f x) (-swap a f x)))
      ([a f x y] (if (host-ref? a) (core a f x y) (-swap a f x y)))
      ([a f x y & more] (if (host-ref? a) (apply core a f x y more) (-swap a f x y more))))))

(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/reset!
  (fn [core] (fn [a v] (if (host-ref? a) (core a v) (-reset a v)))))

(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/compare-and-set!
  (fn [core] (fn [a o n] (if (host-ref? a) (core a o n) (-compare-and-set a o n)))))

(defn- vals-by-swap
  "[old new] of a swap through a type's IAtom: the old value is the one the successful swap's f was given."
  [a f args]
  (let [seen (volatile! nil)
        nv (apply -swap a (fn [old & xs] (vreset! seen old) (apply f old xs)) args)]
    [@seen nv]))

(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/swap-vals!
  (fn [core]
    (fn [a f & args]
      (cond (host-ref? a) (apply core a f args)
            (satisfies? IAtom2 a) (apply -swap-vals a f args)
            :else (let [[x y & more] args]
                    (vals-by-swap a f (cond (nil? args) [] (nil? (next args)) [x]
                                            (nil? more) [x y] :else [x y more])))))))

(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/reset-vals!
  (fn [core]
    (fn [a v]
      (cond (host-ref? a) (core a v)
            (satisfies? IAtom2 a) (-reset-vals a v)
            :else (vals-by-swap a (fn [_] v) [])))))

(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/realized?
  (fn [core] (fn [x] (if (host-ref? x) (core x) (-realized? x)))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; = and hash reaching a type's own; meta on a type
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(def ^:private type-equality (volatile! nil))
(def ^:private own-cache (volatile! {}))

(defn set-type-equality!
  "m: {:equiv (fn [x y]) :hash (fn [x]) :equiv-proto p :hash-proto p} — what = and hash call for a type extending
   the protocol itself (eve's types adapter names eve.core's)."
  [m]
  (vreset! own-cache {})
  (vreset! type-equality m)
  (cpp/eve_host.set_equiv (fn [x y] (let [te @type-equality] (if (and te (extends? (:equiv-proto te) (type-key x)))
                                                                ((:equiv te) x y)
                                                                false))))
  (cpp/eve_host.set_hasher (fn [x] (let [te @type-equality] (if (and te (extends? (:hash-proto te) (type-key x)))
                                                               (bit-and (long ((:hash te) x)) 0xFFFFFFFF)
                                                               (object-addr x))))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; get and assoc reaching a type's own (F-3: an eve collection in an atom, updated with update/assoc, read with (:k m))
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; A deftype instance is an opaque_box to jank, which jank's own assoc and get refused or answered nil: (swap! a
;; update :m e/assoc 2 :b) threw "Objects of type `opaque_box` are not associatively writable" and (:m @a) read nil
;; (int-map-in-an-atom, sorted-set-in-an-atom, sorted-set-disj, eve.deftype.type-id-test's atom rows, tally's).
;; Reads: the eve_obj above declares jank's get, seqable, indexable and call behaviors, whose virtuals — what get,
;; keyword invoke, get-in, contains?, seq (so first, vec, into's source, ...), nth and invoking call — reach the
;; lookup and dispatch hooks. Writes and the rest: jank 0.1 has no behavior for them yet (associatively_writable,
;; countable, conjable, ... are commented out in its object_behavior), so the clojure.core names below are re-rooted
;; (inline dropped) by one table: an eve instance whose own type extends the protocol goes to eve.core's fn,
;; everything else to jank's own — never an eve value back into its own route. jank's precompiled update and
;; assoc-in call assoc through the var, so they follow (measured: eve/probes/jank-xxh3/probe6.cljc).

(def ^:private type-collection (volatile! nil))

(def ^:private op-cache
  "[op tag] -> the table's fn for an instance of that type, or ::none: extends? and type-key on every routed call
   made eve.rrb-vector-test's splicing rows 4.4x slower (136 s → 605 s, jank-v5/v8-targeted.log). Emptied when the
   table is set, as own-cache is when the equality hooks are."
  (volatile! {}))

(defn- op-fn
  "The eve.core fn the table names for op when x is an eve instance whose own type extends op's protocol; else nil."
  [op x]
  (when (cpp/eve_host.is x)
    (let [ck [op (object-tag x)] hit (get @op-cache ck ::miss)]
      (if (identical? hit ::miss)
        (let [r (when-let [[p f] (get @type-collection op)]
                  (when (extends? p (type-key x)) f))]
          (vswap! op-cache assoc ck (if (some? r) r ::none))
          r)
        (when-not (identical? hit ::none) hit)))))

(defn- not-supported [x what]
  (throw (ex-info (str "eve type " (type-key x) " is not " what) {:type (type-key x)})))

(defn nth-of-seq
  "The n'th of a sequential type's seq — the JVM's nth over a list (the types adapter names it for ISequential): out of
   range throws, or answers not-found."
  ([x n] (loop [s (seq x) i 0]
           (cond (nil? s) (throw (ex-info (str "eve: index " n " out of bounds") {:eve/index n}))
                 (== i n) (first s)
                 :else (recur (next s) (inc i)))))
  ([x n nf] (loop [s (seq x) i 0]
              (cond (nil? s) nf
                    (== i n) (first s)
                    :else (recur (next s) (inc i))))))

(defn set-type-collection!
  "m: {op [protocol f]} — for an eve instance whose own type extends the protocol, what jank's get, keyword invoke,
   get-in, contains?, seq, nth, invoking it, and the re-rooted clojure.core names below call (eve's types adapter
   names eve.core's: :lookup ILookup's -lookup, 'seq ISeqable's seq, 'assoc IAssociative's, ...)."
  [m]
  (vreset! op-cache {})
  (vreset! type-collection m)
  (cpp/eve_host.set_lookup (fn [x k nf] (if-let [f (op-fn :lookup x)] (f x k nf) nf)))
  (cpp/eve_host.set_dispatch
   (fn [op x a b]
     (let [op (long op)]
       ;; where Eve's type on the JVM throws, a catchable ex-info here (the identity table's lookups, the reference's
       ;; slots 10 and 11): contains? of a type neither associative nor a set, nth of one neither indexed nor sequential
       ;; (with a not-found too), find of one not associative, a call of one not a fn
       (cond
         (== op 1) (if-let [f (op-fn 'contains? x)] (boolean (f x a)) (not-supported x "associative or a set"))
         (== op 2) (if-let [f (op-fn 'seq x)] (f x) (not-supported x "seqable"))
         (== op 3) (if-let [f (or (op-fn 'nth x) (op-fn 'nth-seq x))] (f x a) (not-supported x "indexed"))
         (== op 4) (if-let [f (or (op-fn 'nth x) (op-fn 'nth-seq x))] (f x a b) (not-supported x "indexed"))
         (== op 5) (if-let [f (op-fn 'invoke x)] (f x a) (not-supported x "a fn"))
         (== op 6) (if-let [f (op-fn 'invoke x)] (f x a b) (not-supported x "a fn"))
         ;; find: [k v] when the associative type has k (select-keys builds through it), else nil
         (== op 7) (if-let [f (op-fn 'find x)] (f x a) (not-supported x "associative"))
         (== op 8) (if-let [f (op-fn 'compare x)] (f x a) (not-supported x "comparable"))
         ;; first and next: a type that is its own seq by its ISeq / INext (-rest's seq without INext); any other
         ;; through its seq (a host seq: never back here)
         (== op 9) (if-let [f (op-fn 'first x)] (f x) (first (seq x)))
         (== op 10) (if-let [f (op-fn 'next x)]
                      (f x)
                      (if-let [f (op-fn 'rest x)] (seq (f x)) (next (seq x))))
         :else (not-supported x (str "an op " op)))))))

(defn- route!
  "clojure.core/sym re-rooted (its inline dropped): an eve instance in first position whose type extends the table's
   protocol for sym goes to the table's fn, everything else to jank's own."
  [sym]
  (when-let [v (ns-resolve 'clojure.core sym)]
    (let [core @v]
      (alter-meta! v dissoc :inline :inline-arities)
      (alter-var-root v (fn [_] (fn ([x] (if-let [f (op-fn sym x)] (f x) (core x)))
                                    ([x a] (if-let [f (op-fn sym x)] (f x a) (core x a)))
                                    ([x a b] (if-let [f (op-fn sym x)] (f x a b) (core x a b)))
                                    ([x a b & more] (if-let [f (op-fn sym x)] (apply f x a b more) (apply core x a b more)))))))))

(doseq [sym '[assoc dissoc conj disj count contains? empty peek pop key val rseq
              transient persistent! conj! assoc! dissoc! disj! pop!
              ;; sequential? too: it is a host class test, blind to an eve instance (an opaque_box is never
              ;; jank's Sequential), and shared code gates on it — EveVector's equiv opens with
              ;; (sequential? other), so an eve vector did not equal ITSELF while a host vector on the
              ;; right passed the same gate ((= v v) false, (= v [1 2 3]) true; measured, Lane M 2026-11-06).
              ;; The types adapter's table answers it for an eve type from its ISequential marker.
              sequential?
              ;; map? and set? are the same blindness one fallback deeper: EveHashMap's and EveHashSet's
              ;; equiv delegate to map-equiv?/set-equiv? when the digest verdict abstains (by-reference
              ;; content), and those open with (map? other)/(set? other) — false for every eve instance,
              ;; so two distinct eve maps/sets holding a by-reference value compared FALSE (measured on
              ;; the release tree on two boxes, eve.digest-cache-test's by-reference row, Lane M 2026-11-06).
              map?]]
  (route! sym))
;; set? is deliberately NOT routed: re-rooting it breaks jank's own core codegen (clojure/core.jank:4523,
;; a bool flows into an oref assignment in a core form compiled against set?'s native answer; measured
;; twice, Lane M 2026-11-06). EveHashSet's equiv fallback therefore still gates on a blind (set? other)
;; for by-reference content — the named sibling in this lane's STATUS, with its repro.

;; = with an eve value on either side compares from the eve side, as the JVM's does: jank's own equal of a jank map
;; and an eve map asked the jank map, which cannot see an eve type — (= {:note [1 2 3]} eve-map) was false where the
;; JVM and babashka say true (eve.tally-test's two-atoms row: the holder's note read back an EveHashMap). An eve
;; value on the left reaches its type's IEquiv through the equiv hook (eve_obj's equal) already.
;; A jank collection holding an eve value compares element by element, as the JVM's equiv does (eq's last arm below):
;; jank's
;; own equal of two vectors compares their elements with jank's equal, which never reaches the eve side — (= ["b1"
;; {:note [1 2 3]}] ["b1" eve-map]) was false (eve.tally-test's two-atoms row, eve.read-region-test's lazy-result
;; row). Only when jank's own answer is false and both are jank maps or sequentials: maps by key, sequentials in
;; lockstep (an infinite seq stops at its first difference).
(def ^:private jank= (deref #'clojure.core/=))
;; jank's own collection predicates, for eve='s fallback: only jank's own maps and sequentials are walked (eve values
;; are answered above it), and a number, keyword or string leaves at once
(def ^:private jank-map? (deref #'clojure.core/map?))
(def ^:private jank-sequential? (deref #'clojure.core/sequential?))
(declare eve=)
(defn- seq-eve= [a b]
  (loop [xs (seq a) ys (seq b)]
    (cond (nil? xs) (nil? ys)
          (nil? ys) false
          (eve= (first xs) (first ys)) (recur (next xs) (next ys))
          :else false)))
(defn- map-eve= [a b]
  (and (== (count a) (count b))
       (every? (fn [e] (let [bv (get b (key e) ::absent)]
                         (and (not (identical? bv ::absent)) (eve= (val e) bv))))
               a)))
(defn- eve= [a b]
  ;; jank's own = first: equal scalars answer at once (an element loop's common case — eve.rrb-vector-test's splicing
  ;; rows compare half a million elements three ways: 136 s before this fallback, 534 s with the checks first)
  (or (jank= a b)
      (let [ea (cpp/eve_host.is a) eb (cpp/eve_host.is b)]
        (cond ea false
              eb (jank= b a)
              (and (jank-map? a) (jank-map? b)) (map-eve= a b)
              (and (jank-sequential? a) (jank-sequential? b)) (seq-eve= a b)
              :else false))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; THE IDENTITY TABLE: jank's core predicates on an eve value, answered by the instance's own type
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; One mechanism with cohost Agent 3's reference (atom.broker agent3/eve-u6-opt3 @ b71aa3e41, IDENTITY-TABLE.md: Lane
;; M's decision, operator-approved, 2026-11-06 11:53 AM ET). jank's own answer is its C++ check, which knows jank's
;; types only: on an eve value coll?, counted?, vector?, map?, set?, seq?, associative?, list? answered false (Lane M's
;; identity audit §C, measured). An eve instance — the one object with a symbol tag — answers each by its type's
;; protocol in eve.core, named in this table; every other value keeps jank's answer, and pays one type compare
;; (opaque_box) first. jank-side code that tells host values from eve values asks object? first, never these alone
;; (eve.core's host-seq?, host-coll?, subvec; sequence below). sorted?, fn? and compare are not in the table: Eve's
;; types answer the first two on the JVM as jank does (false), and compare reaches a type's own IComparable through the
;; one object's compare (B-COMPARE; a type without it throws, as the JVM's).
(def identity-table
  "[jank's predicate, the eve.core protocol an eve instance answers it by, the C++ check of a jank :inline predicate
   (its inline expansion keeps that check for every type but opaque_box), or nil] — one row each."
  [['clojure.core/coll?         'eve.core/ICollection  'cpp/jank.runtime.is_collection]
   ['clojure.core/seq?          'eve.core/ISeq         'cpp/jank.runtime.is_seq]
   ['clojure.core/seqable?      'eve.core/ISeqable     'cpp/jank.runtime.is_seqable]
   ['clojure.core/vector?       'eve.core/IVector      'cpp/jank.runtime.is_vector]
   ['clojure.core/counted?      'eve.core/ICounted     nil]
   ['clojure.core/sequential?   'eve.core/ISequential  nil]
   ['clojure.core/map?          'eve.core/IMap         nil]
   ['clojure.core/set?          'eve.core/ISet         nil]
   ['clojure.core/list?         'eve.core/IList        nil]
   ['clojure.core/associative?  'eve.core/IAssociative nil]
   ['clojure.core/indexed?      'eve.core/IIndexed     nil]
   ['clojure.core/reversible?   'eve.core/IReversible  nil]
   ['clojure.core/ifn?          'eve.core/IFn          nil]])

;; jank 0.1's reversible? and indexed? throw for every value ("TODO: port", core.jank:7012-7022): jank's own values
;; answer as before the table, for every caller (the var's root takes them from here, not from jank's thrower).
(def ^:private host-answers
  {'clojure.core/reversible? (fn [x] (or (vector? x) (sorted? x)))
   'clojure.core/indexed? (fn [x] (vector? x))})

(def ^:private pred-cores
  "jank's own predicate fns, taken before the re-roots below: the answer for every value not an eve instance."
  (merge (into {} (map (fn [[k]] [k @(resolve k)]) identity-table)) host-answers))

(def ^:private pred-protocols
  "The protocol each predicate's row names, resolved at its first eve instance (eve.core loads after this)."
  (volatile! {}))

(defn eve-predicate
  "Predicate k (its clojure.core symbol) of x: an eve instance's by its type's protocol (identity-table), any other
   value's jank's own."
  [k x]
  (if (and (cpp/eve_host.is x) (symbol? (object-tag x)))
    ;; eve.core not loaded (a program of plain deftypes: the completion's own pins): no type extends its protocols
    (if-let [p (or (get @pred-protocols k)
                   (when-let [pv (resolve (second (first (filter #(= k (first %)) identity-table))))]
                     (let [p @pv] (vswap! pred-protocols assoc k p) p)))]
      (boolean (extends? p (object-tag x)))
      false)
    (boolean ((get pred-cores k) x))))

;; coll?, seq?, seqable? and vector? are :inline in jank (core.jank:305, 313, 321, 359): a direct call compiles to
;; jank's C++ check and never reaches the var. Their inline expansion is replaced, not dropped: the C++ check stays the
;; path for every type but opaque_box, which alone goes to eve-predicate (only jank's own headers are named, so a module
;; compiled without this file's C++ expands it; the cast boxes a native argument — (+ a b), a count — as jank's own
;; check does: measured by the reference, .get_type of a native int does not compile). Every row's root takes the same
;; branch, so a call through the var (higher-order, apply) answers alike.
(doseq [[k _ check] identity-table]
  (let [v (resolve k) own (get pred-cores k)]
    (when check
      (alter-meta! v assoc :inline
                   (fn [o]
                     (let [g (gensym "o")]
                       (list 'clojure.core/let [g (list 'cpp/cast 'cpp/jank.runtime.object_ref o)]
                             (list 'if (list 'cpp/== 'cpp/jank.runtime.object_type.opaque_box (list 'cpp/.get_type g))
                                   (list 'clojure.core/boolean (list 'eve.host-completion/eve-predicate (list 'quote k) g))
                                   (list check g)))))))
    (alter-var-root v (fn [_] (fn [x] (if (cpp/== cpp/jank.runtime.object_type.opaque_box (cpp/.get_type x))
                                        (eve-predicate k x)
                                        (own x)))))))

;; into as Clojure 1.10's: with a transducer, a jank collection is built transiently and persistent! runs in the
;; reducing fn's completion — so halt-when's halting input comes back as itself, where jank's into called persistent!
;; on it ("Objects of type `small_integer` are not persistentable": eve.thread-fold-test's registered-transducer row);
;; into an eve collection goes through the routed conj (jank's into conj'd in C++: "Objects of type `opaque_box` are
;; not conjable", eve.thread-fold-group-test).
(let [v #'clojure.core/into core @v]
  (alter-meta! v dissoc :inline :inline-arities)
  (alter-var-root v (fn [_] (fn ([] [])
                                ([to] to)
                                ([to from] (if (cpp/eve_host.is to) (reduce clojure.core/conj to from) (core to from)))
                                ([to xform from]
                                 (if (and (not (cpp/eve_host.is to)) (or (vector? to) (map? to) (set? to)))
                                   (let [tm (meta to)
                                         rf (fn ([coll] (let [r (persistent! coll)] (if tm (with-meta r tm) r)))
                                                ([coll x] (conj! coll x)))]
                                     (transduce xform rf (transient to) from))
                                   (transduce xform clojure.core/conj to from)))))))

;; merge and merge-with as Clojure's, over the routed conj, assoc, get and contains?: jank's own conj in C++, so
;; (merge eve-map m) threw "Objects of type `opaque_box` are not conjable" (eve.thread.domain's measured costs, merged
;; into a runtime's descriptor in the meta-atom: eve.thread-fold-group-test).
(re-root! 'merge (fn ([] nil)
                     ([m] m)
                     ([m & ms] (when (some identity (cons m ms))
                                 (reduce (fn [a b] (clojure.core/conj (or a {}) b)) m ms)))))
(re-root! 'merge-with
          (fn [f & maps]
            (when (some identity maps)
              (let [merge-entry (fn [m e] (let [k (key e) v (val e)]
                                            (if (contains? m k) (assoc m k (f (get m k) v)) (assoc m k v))))
                    merge2 (fn [m1 m2] (reduce merge-entry (or m1 {}) (seq m2)))]
                (reduce merge2 maps)))))

;; reduce-kv takes its collection last
(let [v #'clojure.core/reduce-kv core @v]
  (alter-meta! v dissoc :inline :inline-arities)
  (alter-var-root v (fn [_] (fn [f init coll] (if-let [g (op-fn 'reduce-kv coll)] (g f init coll) (core f init coll))))))

(defn- own? [k x]
  (when-let [te @type-equality]
    (let [c (type-key x) ck [k c] hit (get @own-cache ck ::none)]
      (if (identical? hit ::none)
        (let [r (extends? (get te k) c)] (vswap! own-cache assoc ck r) r)
        hit))))

(def ^:private core-hash hash)

(defn- eq
  "x = y, the slow path: a type's own equivalence first (either side), else eve= (jank's equal, then the element walk
   of two jank maps or sequentials)."
  [x y]
  (cond (and (object? x) (own? :equiv-proto x)) (boolean ((:equiv @type-equality) x y))
        (and (object? y) (own? :equiv-proto y)) (boolean ((:equiv @type-equality) y x))
        ;; neither is a type with its own equivalence: jank's own =, and where it says no for two jank maps or
        ;; sequentials, element by element through this = (eve= above: a jank vector holding an eve map)
        :else (eve= x y)))

(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/=
  (fn [_]
    (fn ([_] true)
      ([x y] (if (cpp/eve_host.eq_plain x y) (cpp/jank.runtime.equal x y) (eq x y)))
      ([x y & more] (if (eq x y)
                      (if (next more) (recur y (first more) (next more)) (eq y (first more)))
                      false)))))
;; No :inline for the 2-ary call: measured, an inline expansion of this fast path (jank's own C++ only) answered
;; (= i 5) in 104 ns against 118 through the var, and (= :a :b) in 152 against 152 (probe3 P5/P6 vs P18/P19) — not
;; worth an expansion every module compiles.
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/not= (fn [_] (fn ([_] false) ([x y] (not (= x y))) ([x y & more] (not (apply = x y more))))))
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/hash
  (fn [_] (fn [x] (if (and (object? x) (own? :hash-proto x))
                    (bit-and (long ((:hash @type-equality) x)) 0xFFFFFFFF)
                    (core-hash x)))))

(def ^:private core-meta meta)
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/meta (fn [_] (fn [x] (if (object? x) nil (core-meta x)))))

;; a printer for every instance: jank's str / pr-str / println reach it through the C++ object
(def ^:private printers (atom {}))

(defn set-printer!
  "f prints an instance of the type tagged tag: (f x) → a string."
  [tag f]
  (swap! printers assoc tag f))

(cpp/eve_host.set_printer
 (fn [x]
   (let [tag (object-tag x)]
     (if-let [f (get @printers tag)]
       (f x)
       (str "#object[" tag " 0x" (object-addr x) "]")))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; deftype
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defn- mutable-field? [f]
  (let [m (meta f)] (or (:mutable m) (:unsynchronized-mutable m) (:volatile-mutable m))))

(defn- binding-syms
  "The symbols a binding form (a symbol, or a destructuring vector or map) binds."
  [b]
  (cond (symbol? b) (if (= '& b) [] [b])
        (vector? b) (mapcat binding-syms b)
        (map? b) (concat (mapcat binding-syms (remove keyword? (keys b)))
                         (mapcat (fn [[k v]] (when (#{:keys :syms :strs} k) (map #(symbol (name %)) v))) b)
                         (when-let [a (:as b)] [a]))
        :else []))

(def ^:private bound-forms
  "The forms whose binding vector the cell walk reads (a name they bind shadows a field)."
  '#{let let* loop loop* when-let if-let when-some if-some when-first binding
     clojure.core/let clojure.core/loop clojure.core/when-let clojure.core/if-let
     clojure.core/when-some clojure.core/if-some clojure.core/binding})

(def ^:private special-forms
  "jank's special forms (special-symbol? is a TODO stub in its core)."
  '#{def if do let* loop* fn* recur quote var throw try catch finally set! letfn* case* new .})

(defn- cells
  "A method body with each cell field (a symbol in cs) read through deref and set! through vreset!: a name a let,
   loop, fn or binding form binds is left alone where it is bound."
  [form cs]
  (letfn [(walk [form shadow]
            (cond
              (and (symbol? form) (contains? cs form) (not (contains? shadow form)))
              (list 'clojure.core/deref form)

              (not (seq? form))
              (cond (vector? form) (with-meta (mapv #(walk % shadow) form) (meta form))
                    (map? form) (with-meta (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(walk k shadow) (walk v shadow)])) form)
                                  (meta form))
                    (set? form) (with-meta (set (map #(walk % shadow) form)) (meta form))
                    :else form)

              (empty? form) form
              (contains? '#{quote var} (first form)) form

              ;; a macro call is expanded first (a cell field it names, (caching-hash this f hash__), is the place it
              ;; set!s after expansion, not a read)
              (and (symbol? (first form)) (not (contains? shadow (first form)))
                   (not (contains? special-forms (first form)))
                   (not (contains? bound-forms (first form)))
                   (when-let [v (resolve (first form))] (and (var? v) (:macro (meta v)))))
              (walk (macroexpand-1 form) shadow)

              (and (= 'set! (first form)) (symbol? (second form)) (contains? cs (second form))
                   (not (contains? shadow (second form))))
              (list 'clojure.core/vreset! (second form) (walk (nth form 2) shadow))

              (contains? bound-forms (first form))
              (let [[op bvec & body] form
                    [bs shadow'] (reduce (fn [[acc sh] [b init]]
                                           [(conj acc b (walk init sh)) (into sh (binding-syms b))])
                                         [[] shadow] (partition 2 bvec))]
                (with-meta (list* op bs (map #(walk % shadow') body)) (meta form)))

              (contains? '#{fn fn* clojure.core/fn} (first form))
              (let [[op & more] form
                    [nm more] (if (symbol? (first more)) [(first more) (rest more)] [nil more])
                    sh (cond-> shadow nm (conj nm))]
                (with-meta (concat (cond-> [op] nm (conj nm))
                                   (if (vector? (first more))
                                     (let [[args & body] more sh (into sh (binding-syms args))]
                                       (cons args (map #(walk % sh) body)))
                                     (map (fn [[args & body]]
                                            (let [sh (into sh (binding-syms args))]
                                              (list* args (map #(walk % sh) body))))
                                          more)))
                  (meta form)))

              :else (with-meta (apply list (map #(walk % shadow) form)) (meta form))))]
    (walk form #{})))

(defn- occurs?
  "Whether symbol s occurs anywhere in form (a field a body never names is not bound for it)."
  [s form]
  (cond (= s form) true
        (or (seq? form) (vector? form) (set? form)) (boolean (some #(occurs? s %) form))
        (map? form) (boolean (some #(or (occurs? s (key %)) (occurs? s (val %))) form))
        :else false))

(defn- untag [x] (if (and (symbol? x) (meta x)) (with-meta x nil) x))

(defn- method-arities
  "A protocol's methods as extend-type takes them: one entry per name, its arities from every entry with that name
   (deftype lists an arity per entry), each body with the fields it names bound from this (field i is
   (nth (object-fields this) i))."
  [methods fields cs]
  (for [[nm entries] (group-by first methods)]
    (cons nm
          (for [[_ args & body] entries
                :let [args (mapv untag args)
                      ;; a this named _ is renamed: a later _ parameter would shadow it ((m [_ _] field) read nil);
                      ;; when _ is the this alone, the body's _ is the this, as in Clojure ((valAt [_ k] (cmp-of _))
                      ;; in an external library's type: "The symbol `_` could not be resolved" without it)
                      self_ (and (= '_ (first args)) (not (some #{'_} (rest args))) (occurs? '_ body))
                      args (if (= '_ (first args)) (assoc args 0 (gensym "this__")) args)
                      this (first args)
                      shadow (set (binding-syms args))
                      used (filter #(and (not (contains? shadow %)) (occurs? % body)) fields)
                      body (map #(cells % (apply disj cs shadow)) body)
                      binds (vec (concat (when self_ ['_ this])
                                         (mapcat (fn [f] [f (list 'clojure.core/nth (list 'eve.host-completion/object-fields this)
                                                                 (first (keep-indexed (fn [i x] (when (= x f) i)) fields)))])
                                                 used)))]]
            (list args
                  (if (seq binds)
                    (list* 'clojure.core/let binds body)
                    (cons 'do body)))))))

(def ^:private dropped-protocols
  "What a deftype here takes no impls for: Object's methods (printing is the types adapter's: set-printer!),
   and clojure.lang.IKeywordLookup — an optimization interface with no eve.core counterpart (keyword
   lookup dispatches through ILookup here); its getLookupThunk method is discarded by the same
   equals/hashCode-only salvage that handles a dropped Object group's methods."
  '#{Object java.lang.Object clojure.lang.IKeywordLookup})

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; deftype specs naming clojure.lang interfaces (F-JANK-CLJFACE-DEFTYPE)
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; A vanilla :clj-face deftype names JVM interfaces and Java method names (datascript.lru:
;; clojure.lang.ILookup (valAt ...), clojure.lang.Associative (assoc ...); datascript.impl.entity:
;; Seqable / Associative / ILookup / IFn). On the JVM those are the host's own machinery; here the
;; seat's answer to each is the eve.core protocol of the same meaning — the one registry jank's get,
;; the routed clojure.core names and the eve_obj dispatch hooks consult (the types adapter's table).
;; The deftype macro presents such a declaration in the full form the seat accepts: each clojure.lang
;; spec is completed to the eve.core protocol(s) its methods belong to (a piecemeal list — ILookup
;; alone, Associative alone — is completed by its methods: Associative's valAt belongs to ILookup),
;; Java method names become the protocols' (valAt → -lookup, containsKey → -contains-key?; the
;; eve.deftype-proto jvm->cljs table), and method bodies are rewritten where they call the JVM surface
;; directly: (.valAt x k) → (get x k), (.containsKey x k) → (contains? x k), (.entryAt x k) → (find x k)
;; (find is synthesized from -contains-key? + -lookup by the types adapter, so an entryAt method itself
;; is dropped), (clojure.lang.MapEntry. k v) → [k v], (UnsupportedOperationException. msg) → (ex-info
;; msg {}). Object's equals and hashCode — dropped with the rest of Object until now — are kept as
;; IEquiv/-equiv and IHash/-hash, which is what = and hash reach through the equality hooks; toString
;; stays the printer layer's. A spec naming anything else passes through unchanged.

(defn clj-proto
  "eve.core's protocol atom for a protocol name (ILookup, IAssociative, ...): what a clojure.lang
   interface in a deftype spec translates to. eve.core is required on first use. eve.types is
   required unconditionally: its set-type-collection! call at load is what routes core fns
   (assoc/get/...) to the protocols for eve objects — Eve's own deftype macros pull eve.types
   in at their expansion time, but a completion deftype's expansions must not depend on that
   having happened first (eve.core can be loaded with the table still empty)."
  [pname]
  (require 'eve.types)
  (if-let [v (when (find-ns 'eve.core) (ns-resolve 'eve.core pname))]
    @v
    (do (require 'eve.core)
        @(ns-resolve 'eve.core pname))))

(def ^:private clj-method-dest
  "A JVM method name → [eve.core protocol, its method name]; entryAt → nil (find synthesizes it).
   compare → [IFn -invoke]: java.util.Comparator has no eve.core protocol — a Comparator's seat
   is a plain 2-arg fn (datascript.db's defcomp builds exactly that on the non-JVM faces), so
   its compare method is the fn's invoke, and the reified object is callable as one."
  '{valAt [ILookup -lookup] assoc [IAssociative -assoc] containsKey [IAssociative -contains-key?]
    entryAt nil
    seq [ISeqable -seq] count [ICounted -count] invoke [IFn -invoke] cons [ICollection -conj]
    empty [IEmptyableCollection -empty] equiv [IEquiv -equiv] hasheq [IHash -hash]
    nth [IIndexed -nth] without [IMap -dissoc] peek [IStack -peek] pop [IStack -pop]
    meta [IMeta -meta] withMeta [IWithMeta -with-meta] deref [IDeref -deref]
    reduce [IReduce -reduce] kvreduce [IKVReduce -kv-reduce] rseq [IReversible -rseq]
    equals [IEquiv -equiv] hashCode [IHash -hash] compare [IFn -invoke]})

(def ^:private clj-iface-proto
  "A clojure.lang interface → its primary eve.core protocol (the home of a method the table lacks)."
  '{clojure.lang.ILookup ILookup clojure.lang.Associative IAssociative clojure.lang.Seqable ISeqable
    clojure.lang.Counted ICounted clojure.lang.IFn IFn clojure.lang.IHashEq IHash
    clojure.lang.IPersistentCollection ICollection clojure.lang.IPersistentMap IMap
    clojure.lang.Indexed IIndexed clojure.lang.IMeta IMeta clojure.lang.IObj IWithMeta
    clojure.lang.IDeref IDeref clojure.lang.IReduce IReduce clojure.lang.IKVReduce IKVReduce
    clojure.lang.Reversible IReversible clojure.lang.IPersistentStack IStack
    clojure.lang.IPersistentVector IVector clojure.lang.IPersistentSet ISet
    java.util.Comparator IFn})

(def ^:private clj-data-proto-names
  "clojure.data's protocols by their spec name: jank ships clojure.data natively with the protocol
   FUNCTIONS (equality-partition, diff-similar) but no protocol vars, so a deftype spec naming
   clojure.data/EqualityPartition has no var to resolve and nothing to extend."
  '{clojure.data/EqualityPartition EqualityPartition clojure.data/Diff Diff})

(def ^:private clj-data-protos (atom {}))

(defn clj-data-proto
  "The seat's protocol atom for a clojure.data protocol, built on first use: registrations (a
   deftype's equality-partition / diff-similar methods) land here. Calls still dispatch through
   jank's native clojure.data fns, which do not consult these registrations."
  [pname]
  (or (get @clj-data-protos pname)
      (let [p (atom {:name (symbol "clojure.data" (name pname)) :fns {} :impls [] :sat {}})]
        (swap! clj-data-protos assoc pname p)
        p)))

(def ^:private clj-method-xlate
  "A JVM method name → the seat's dispatching name for it, in a (.name target args...) form whose
   target is an ordinary value: the :clj face's methods on collections and shimmed classes, stated
   once. valAt/containsKey/entryAt are clojure.lang's own; first/next/cons are ISeq/IPersistentCollection's;
   equals/compareTo/toString/size are Object's and the collections'; get is List.get/Map.get (one
   helper decides by the key); add is List.add on the ArrayList shim; write is Writer.write;
   getMostSignificantBits/getLeastSignificantBits are UUID's, over its [msb lsb] form."
  '{valAt clojure.core/get containsKey clojure.core/contains? entryAt clojure.core/find
    first clojure.core/first next clojure.core/next cons clojure.core/conj
    equals clojure.core/= compareTo clojure.core/compare toString clojure.core/str
    size clojure.core/count
    get eve.host-completion/jvm-get add eve.host-completion/jvm-add write eve.host-completion/jvm-write
    getMostSignificantBits eve.host-completion/uuid-msb getLeastSignificantBits eve.host-completion/uuid-lsb
    getClass clojure.core/type getName clojure.core/name
    ;; startsWith is String's, answered by clojure.string (eve.atom's eve-class?
    ;; screen, landed on the release line after the collate fork: the merged
    ;; tree's first jank analysis wall)
    startsWith clojure.string/starts-with?})

(def ^:private clj-ctor-xlate
  "A JVM class name (the head of a (Class. args...) form, dot stripped) → how the seat builds it:
   the exception classes are ex-info; MapEntry is its [k v] entry vector; ArrayList and UUID are
   the completion's shims. A constructor naming anything else — a deftype of the file's own, above
   all — passes through unchanged."
  '{clojure.lang.MapEntry clojure.core/vector
    UnsupportedOperationException eve.host-completion/ex-info-ctor
    IllegalArgumentException eve.host-completion/ex-info-ctor
    IndexOutOfBoundsException eve.host-completion/ex-info-ctor
    java.lang.IndexOutOfBoundsException eve.host-completion/ex-info-ctor
    Exception eve.host-completion/ex-info-ctor
    java.util.ArrayList eve.host-completion/array-list
    UUID eve.host-completion/uuid-new})

(def ^:private clj-class-value-syms
  "Dotted class names a vanilla :clj body may name in VALUE position (a :tag value in a meta
   map — datascript.db's patch-tag assocs java.lang.Boolean — a map/vector member, a defn
   hint's target): on the JVM the symbol resolves to the class; here there is no class for the
   analyzer to resolve, and the seat's own uses of such a name are as data (a tag, a type key),
   so clj-face quotes it. Static-call heads (clojure.lang.Util/hashCombine — the symbol carries
   a slash) and constructor heads (…MapEntry. — handled by the ctor clause) are not in this set."
  '#{clojure.lang.Seqable clojure.lang.ILookup clojure.lang.Associative clojure.lang.IPersistentSet
     clojure.lang.IPersistentList clojure.lang.IPersistentStack clojure.lang.IMeta clojure.lang.IReduce
     clojure.lang.ISeq clojure.lang.IPersistentVector clojure.lang.IPersistentMap
     clojure.lang.IPersistentCollection clojure.lang.Counted clojure.lang.IFn clojure.lang.IAtom
     clojure.lang.IDeref clojure.lang.Indexed clojure.lang.Sequential clojure.lang.IMapEntry
     clojure.lang.ITransientCollection clojure.lang.IEditableCollection clojure.lang.IObj
     clojure.lang.IHashEq clojure.lang.IReduceInit clojure.lang.IKVReduce clojure.lang.MapEntry
     java.lang.Object java.lang.String java.lang.Boolean java.lang.Long java.lang.Integer
     java.lang.Double java.lang.Character java.lang.Number java.lang.Comparable
     java.lang.StringBuilder java.lang.Exception java.util.Collection java.util.List
     java.util.ListIterator java.util.Iterator java.util.Map java.util.Set java.util.Date
     java.util.UUID java.util.Comparator})

(defn clj-face
  "A form of :clj-face (vanilla JVM) code with its direct JVM-surface calls rewritten to the seat's
   dispatching names: (.name target args...) and (. target (name args...)) method forms by
   clj-method-xlate, (Class. args...) constructors by clj-ctor-xlate. Quoted forms are data and
   pass untouched; anything unrecognized passes through unchanged, to fail honestly if reached."
  [form]
  (cond (seq? form)
        (let [h (first form)]
          (cond (= h 'quote) form
                ;; (set! *warn-on-reflection* v): a compiler-flag statement of the :clj face; this
                ;; host has no reflection warnings to toggle, so the statement is read and dropped
                (and (= h 'set!) (symbol? (second form))
                     (= \* (first (name (second form))))) nil
                ;; (instance? <JVM interface name> x): the name is no value here; the question is
                ;; the value's type against the interface's eve.core protocol (clj-instance?)
                (and (contains? '#{instance? clojure.core/instance?} h)
                     (symbol? (second form))
                     (or (contains? clj-class-protos (class-simple-name (second form))) (contains? clj-class-preds (class-simple-name (second form)))))
                (list 'eve.host-completion/clj-instance? (list 'quote (second form)) (clj-face (nth form 2)))
                ;; (clojure.lang.Util/hashCombine x y): a static call of the :clj face — the
                ;; seat's own mixer (util-hash-combine), as the :cljs face's hash-combine
                ;; answers the same defn there
                ;; (Double/isNaN x): a wrapper-class static of the :clj face — the host's
                ;; own NaN test answers it (datascript.serialize's number dispatch)
                (and (= h 'Double/isNaN) (= 2 (count form)))
                (list 'eve.host-completion/clj-nan? (clj-face (nth form 1)))
                                (and (= h 'clojure.lang.Util/hashCombine) (= 3 (count form)))
                (list 'eve.host-completion/util-hash-combine
                      (clj-face (nth form 1)) (clj-face (nth form 2)))
                ;; (. clojure.lang.Util (hasheq x)): the seat's hash, as the :cljs face's
                ;; (hash x) answers datascript.db's ihash there
                (and (= h '.) (= (second form) 'clojure.lang.Util)
                     (seq? (nth form 2)) (= 'hasheq (first (nth form 2))))
                (list 'clojure.core/hash (clj-face (second (nth form 2))))
                ;; (.compare cmp a b): a Comparator call — the seat's Comparator is a plain
                ;; 2-arg fn (the reify translation above), so the call is the call itself
                (and (= h '.) (seq? (nth form 2)) (= 'compare (first (nth form 2)))
                     (= 2 (count (nth form 2))))
                (apply list (clj-face (second form)) (map clj-face (rest (nth form 2))))
                ;; (defmethod print-method T [x w] body...): this seat has no print-method
                ;; var to extend (jank's core is fixed; printing an instance is the types
                ;; adapter's registry: set-printer! under the type's tag — the keyword its
                ;; deftype var holds), so the method becomes the type's printer: the body
                ;; runs against a string writer (print-via-string-writer). The writer arg
                ;; name is the form's own; the vector is passed untranslated (its symbols
                ;; are binding names, and a ^Tag on the value is read and dropped as data —
                ;; its class symbols must never be walked as values).
                (and (= h 'defmethod) (= (second form) 'print-method) (symbol? (nth form 2))
                     (vector? (nth form 3)))
                (list 'eve.host-completion/set-printer! (list 'quote (nth form 2))
                      (list 'fn [(first (nth form 3))]
                            (list 'eve.host-completion/print-via-string-writer
                                  (first (nth form 3))
                                  (list 'quote (nth form 3))
                                  (list 'quote (apply list (map clj-face (nthnext form 4)))))))
                ;; (. target (name args...)) / (. target name args...): normalize to (.name target args...)
                (= h '.)
                (let [target (second form) r (nthnext form 2)
                      m (first r)]
                  (if (or (seq? m) (and (symbol? m) (contains? clj-method-xlate m)))
                    (clj-face (apply list (symbol (str "." (if (seq? m) (first m) m))) target
                                     (if (seq? m) (rest m) (rest r))))
                    (apply list (map clj-face form))))
                ;; (.name target args...)
                (and (symbol? h) (> (count (name h)) 1) (= "." (subs (name h) 0 1)))
                (if-let [f (get clj-method-xlate (symbol (subs (name h) 1)))]
                  (apply list f (map clj-face (rest form)))
                  (apply list (map clj-face form)))
                ;; (Class. args...)
                (and (symbol? h) (> (count (name h)) 1) (= "." (subs (name h) (dec (count (name h))))))
                (if-let [f (get clj-ctor-xlate (symbol (subs (name h) 0 (dec (count (name h))))))]
                  (apply list f (map clj-face (rest form)))
                  (apply list (map clj-face form)))
                ;; a type-spec form (deftype & kin): its direct symbol elements are spec /
                ;; protocol NAMES — data of the type DSL, never values — so they pass
                ;; unquoted (the value-quote below would hand the spec parser a (quote …)
                ;; seq where it expects a symbol: measured, ds-collate DB3); subforms
                ;; (method entries, bodies) are walked as their own forms as usual
                :else (if (contains? '#{deftype eve-deftype defrecord reify extend-type
                                        extend-protocol defprotocol eve-extend-type
                                        defrecord-updatable}
                                     ;; the head matched by NAME: a spec head is spelled
                                     ;; qualified at its call sites (edt/deftype,
                                     ;; eve.deftype-proto.macros/deftype, clojure.core/deftype),
                                     ;; and the qualified symbol is not in the set - the generic
                                     ;; walk then quotes the spec's class-name protocol heads
                                     ;; (clojure.lang.Counted becomes (quote clojure.lang.Counted)),
                                     ;; the spec parser drops the leading group and files each
                                     ;; (quote ...) as a bogus method entry (name quote, args the
                                     ;; bare class symbol) in the preceding group: every
                                     ;; JVM-named group of every eve deftype corrupted on this
                                     ;; seat, crashing where such an entry reaches the deftype
                                     ;; machinery (eve.rseq's RSeq: F-JANK-FACE-SPEC-HEADS)
                                     (if (symbol? h) (symbol (name h)) h))
                        (apply list (map (fn [el] (if (symbol? el) el (clj-face el))) form))
                        (apply list (map clj-face form)))))
        (vector? form) (mapv clj-face form)
        (map? form) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(clj-face k) (clj-face v)]) form))
        (set? form) (into #{} (map clj-face form))
        ;; a dotted class name in value position: data here, not a class (see
        ;; clj-class-value-syms) — quoted, so the analyzer never tries to resolve it
        (symbol? form) (if (contains? clj-class-value-syms form) (list 'quote form) form)
        :else form))

(defn- clj-body
  "A deftype method body with its direct JVM-surface calls rewritten: clj-face, at method scale."
  [form]
  (clj-face form))

(defn- clj-rewrite-entry
  "A method entry ((name [args] body...) or (name ([args] body...) ...)) with bodies rewritten."
  [[mname & arities]]
  (cons mname
        (if (vector? (first arities))
          (cons (first arities) (map clj-body (rest arities)))
          (map (fn [arity] (cons (first arity) (map clj-body (rest arity)))) arities))))

(defn- translate-impls
  "parse-impls' groups, plus a dropped Object group's methods, in the seat's form: [[proto methods]...]
   where proto is the original spec symbol, or a (clj-proto 'Name) form for a translated group."
  [impls object-methods]
  (let [by-dest (fn [entries]
                  (reduce (fn [acc e]
                            (let [dest (get clj-method-dest (first e) ::unknown)]
                              (cond (nil? dest) acc
                                    (= ::unknown dest) (update acc ::unknown (fnil conj []) e)
                                    :else (update acc dest (fnil conj []) e))))
                          {} entries))
        emit (fn [by-dest fallback]
               (for [[dest entries] by-dest]
                 (if (= ::unknown dest)
                   [fallback (map clj-rewrite-entry entries)]
                   [(list 'eve.host-completion/clj-proto (list 'quote (first dest)))
                    (map (fn [e] (clj-rewrite-entry (cons (second dest) (rest e)))) entries)])))]
    (concat
      (mapcat (fn [[p methods]]
                (cond (contains? clj-iface-proto p)
                      (emit (by-dest methods)
                            (list 'eve.host-completion/clj-proto (list 'quote (get clj-iface-proto p))))
                      (contains? clj-data-proto-names p)
                      [[(list 'eve.host-completion/clj-data-proto (list 'quote (get clj-data-proto-names p)))
                        (map clj-rewrite-entry methods)]]
                      :else
                      [[p (map clj-rewrite-entry methods)]]))
              impls)
      (emit (by-dest (filter (fn [e] (contains? '#{equals hashCode} (first e))) object-methods)) nil))))

(defmacro deftype
  "(deftype T [fields...] Protocol (method [this ...] body...) ...): T names its tag (a symbol, this namespace's
   T); ->T, T. and T__make build an instance, a cell made for each mutable field."
  [type-name fields & specs]
  (let [tag (symbol (str *ns*) (name type-name))
        names (mapv untag fields)
        cs (set (map untag (filter mutable-field? fields)))
        raw-impls (parse-impls specs)
        object-methods (mapcat (fn [[p ms]] (if (contains? dropped-protocols p) ms [])) raw-impls)
        impls (translate-impls (remove #(contains? dropped-protocols (first %)) raw-impls)
                               object-methods)
        args (mapv #(symbol (str "a" %)) (range (count names)))
        cell (fn [f a] (if (contains? cs f) `(clojure.core/volatile! ~a) a))
        ;; jank caps a fixed-arity fn at 10 parameters (measured: "This function has too many parameters. The max is
        ;; 10"): a type of more fields (an eve-deftype's slab-off__ and sio__ among them) builds from a rest argument
        rest-args (gensym "args")
        factory (if (<= (count names) 10)
                  `(fn ~args (eve.host-completion/make-object '~tag ~(mapv cell names args)))
                  `(fn [& ~rest-args] (eve.host-completion/make-object '~tag
                                        ~(mapv (fn [f i] (cell f `(clojure.core/nth ~rest-args ~i))) names (range (count names))))))]
    `(do (def ~type-name '~tag)
         (swap! eve.host-completion/type-fields assoc '~tag '~names)
         (swap! eve.host-completion/type-mutable assoc '~tag '~cs)
         (swap! eve.host-completion/type-field-index assoc '~tag (eve.host-completion/field-entries '~names '~cs))
         (def ~(symbol (str (name type-name) "__make")) ~factory)
         ;; ->T and T. by intern, not def: an eve-deftype's expansion defines ->T again (its constructor) in the same
         ;; top-level form, and jank binds a var defined twice in one form to the FIRST definition when the second's
         ;; deferred fn is compiled at its first call (measured: upstream defect 26). intern leaves one def in the form; the
         ;; declare (a def without a value, which does not take part) lets a form that names ->T right after resolve it.
         (declare ~(symbol (str "->" (name type-name))) ~(symbol (str (name type-name) ".")))
         (intern '~(symbol (namespace tag)) '~(symbol (str "->" (name type-name))) ~factory)
         (intern '~(symbol (namespace tag)) '~(symbol (str (name type-name) ".")) ~factory)
         ~@(for [[p methods] impls]
             `(eve.host-completion/extend '~tag ~p ~(method-map (method-arities methods names cs))))
         ~type-name)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; defrecord: a map carrying its type in metadata
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defmacro defrecord
  "(defrecord R [fields...] Protocol (method ...) ...): an instance is a map of its fields with {:eve/record 'ns/R}
   in its metadata; ->R and map->R build one; R names its tag."
  [type-name fields & specs]
  (let [tag (symbol (str *ns*) (name type-name))
        names (mapv untag fields)
        raw-impls (parse-impls specs)
        object-methods (mapcat (fn [[p ms]] (if (contains? dropped-protocols p) ms [])) raw-impls)
        impls (translate-impls (remove #(contains? dropped-protocols (first %)) raw-impls)
                               object-methods)]
    `(do (def ~type-name '~tag)
         (defn ~(symbol (str "->" (name type-name))) ~names
           (with-meta ~(zipmap (map keyword names) names) {:eve/record '~tag}))
         (defn ~(symbol (str "map->" (name type-name))) [m#]
           (with-meta (merge ~(zipmap (map keyword names) (repeat nil)) m#) {:eve/record '~tag}))
         (def ~(symbol (str (name type-name) ".")) ~(symbol (str "->" (name type-name))))
         ~@(for [[p methods] impls]
             `(eve.host-completion/extend '~tag ~p ~(method-map (for [[nm args & body] methods
                                                   :let [args (mapv untag args)
                                                         ;; _ the this alone: the body's _ is the this (deftype's rule)
                                                         self_ (and (= '_ (first args)) (not (some #{'_} (rest args)))
                                                                    (occurs? '_ body))
                                                         args (if (= '_ (first args)) (assoc args 0 (gensym "this__")) args)]]
                                              (list* nm args
                                                     (let [this (first args)
                                                           used (filter #(occurs? % body) names)
                                                           binds (vec (concat (when self_ ['_ this])
                                                                              (mapcat (fn [f] [f (list (keyword f) this)]) used)))]
                                                       (if (seq binds)
                                                         [(list* 'clojure.core/let binds body)]
                                                         body)))))))
         ~type-name)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; reify
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(def ^:private reify-tags (atom {}))

(defmacro reify
  "(reify Protocol (method [this ...] body...) ...): an instance whose one field is a map of its closures; its tag
   made once for this form (at its expansion), its methods extended to the tag, each calling the closure."
  [& specs]
  (let [impls (remove #(contains? dropped-protocols (first %)) (parse-impls specs))
        k [(str *ns*) (pr-str specs)]
        tag (or (get @reify-tags k)
                (let [t (symbol (str *ns*) (str (gensym "reify__")))]
                  (swap! reify-tags assoc k t)
                  t))
        fns (into {} (for [[_ methods] impls [nm entries] (group-by first methods)]
                       [(list 'quote nm)
                        (cons 'clojure.core/fn (for [[_ args & body] entries] (list* (mapv untag args) body)))]))]
    `(do ~@(for [[p methods] impls]
             `(eve.host-completion/extend '~tag ~p
                ~(into {} (for [[nm entries] (group-by first methods)]
                            [(keyword (name nm))
                             (cons 'clojure.core/fn
                                   (for [[_ args] entries
                                         :let [as (vec (repeatedly (count args) #(gensym "a")))]]
                                     (list as (list* (list 'clojure.core/get
                                                           (list 'clojure.core/nth (list 'eve.host-completion/object-fields (first as)) 0)
                                                           (list 'quote nm))
                                                     as))))]))))
         (eve.host-completion/make-object '~tag [~fns]))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Collection hashes (Clojure's Murmur3 mixing: jank's core leaves them as TODO), locking, sorted walks
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defn- imul32 [a b] (i32 (* (i32 a) (i32 b))))
(defn- rotl32 [x r] (let [u (bit-and (long x) 0xFFFFFFFF)]
                      (i32 (bit-or (bit-shift-left u r) (unsigned-bit-shift-right u (- 32 r))))))
(defn- ushr32 [x n] (unsigned-bit-shift-right (bit-and (long x) 0xFFFFFFFF) n))

(defn- fmix32 [h len]
  (let [h (bit-xor h len)
        h (bit-xor h (ushr32 h 16))
        h (imul32 h 0x85ebca6b)
        h (bit-xor h (ushr32 h 13))
        h (imul32 h 0xc2b2ae35)
        h (bit-xor h (ushr32 h 16))]
    (i32 h)))

(defn mix-collection-hash
  "Clojure's Murmur3 mixCollHash: a collection's hash from its basis and count (a signed 32-bit value)."
  [hash-basis count]
  (let [k1 (-> hash-basis (imul32 0xcc9e2d51) (rotl32 15) (imul32 0x1b873593))
        h1 (bit-xor 0 k1)
        h1 (-> h1 (rotl32 13) (imul32 5) (i32) (+ 0xe6546b64) (i32))]
    (fmix32 h1 count)))

(defn hash-ordered-coll [coll]
  (loop [n 0 h 1 s (seq coll)]
    (if s
      (recur (inc n) (i32 (+ (imul32 31 h) (i32 (hash (first s))))) (next s))
      (mix-collection-hash h n))))

(defn hash-unordered-coll [coll]
  (loop [n 0 h 0 s (seq coll)]
    (if s
      (recur (inc n) (i32 (+ h (i32 (hash (first s))))) (next s))
      (mix-collection-hash h n))))

(re-root! 'mix-collection-hash mix-collection-hash)
(re-root! 'hash-ordered-coll hash-ordered-coll)
(re-root! 'hash-unordered-coll hash-unordered-coll)

(defmacro locking
  "One thread for now (thread/none): the body. The thread adapter's lock replaces it (J3)."
  [_x & body]
  `(do ~@body))

(re-root! 'requiring-resolve (fn [sym] (or (resolve sym) (do (require (symbol (namespace sym))) (resolve sym)))))
;; reversible? and indexed?: the identity table (above) — an eve instance by its type, jank's own values as before
(re-root! 'rseq (fn [x] (seq (reverse x))))
(re-root! 'into-array (fn ([aseq] (object-array (vec aseq))) ([_type aseq] (object-array (vec aseq)))))
;; sort and sort-by of an empty collection answer a native_vector_sequence whose first segfaults ((first (sort []))
;; and (str/join " " (sort [])) end the process, exit 139: measured; seq and count of it are fine — upstream 25). An
;; empty collection sorts to (); the rest is jank's own.
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/sort
  (fn [core] (fn ([coll] (if (seq coll) (core coll) ())) ([cmp coll] (if (seq coll) (core cmp coll) ())))))
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/sort-by
  (fn [core] (fn ([k coll] (if (seq coll) (core k coll) ())) ([k cmp coll] (if (seq coll) (core k cmp coll) ())))))

;; subseq and rsubseq: a walk of seq and rseq with the collection's comparator (as glojure's completion)
(defn- sorted-key [sc e] (if (map? sc) (key e) e))
(defn- bound [sc test k]
  (fn [e] (test (compare (sorted-key sc e) k) 0)))

(re-root! 'subseq
  (fn ([sc test k]
       (let [in? (bound sc test k)]
         (seq (if (#{> >=} test) (drop-while (complement in?) (seq sc)) (take-while in? (seq sc))))))
    ([sc start-test start-key end-test end-key]
     (seq (take-while (bound sc end-test end-key)
                      (drop-while (complement (bound sc start-test start-key)) (seq sc)))))))

(re-root! 'rsubseq
  (fn ([sc test k]
       (let [in? (bound sc test k) rs (reverse (seq sc))]
         (seq (if (#{< <=} test) (drop-while (complement in?) rs) (take-while in? rs)))))
    ([sc start-test start-key end-test end-key]
     (let [rs (reverse (seq sc))]
       (seq (take-while (bound sc start-test start-key)
                        (drop-while (complement (bound sc end-test end-key)) rs)))))))

;; sequence with a transducer: Clojure's lazy one (jank's is a TODO stub)
(defn- xf-sequence [xform inputs step-in]
  (let [out (volatile! [])
        rf (xform (fn ([acc] acc) ([acc x] (vswap! out conj x) acc)))
        drain (fn [] (let [v @out] (vreset! out []) v))
        step (fn step [s]
               (lazy-seq
                (loop [s s]
                  (if (seq @out)
                    (concat (drain) (step s))
                    (if-let [s (seq s)]
                      (if (reduced? (step-in rf (first s)))
                        (do (rf nil) (seq (drain)))
                        (recur (rest s)))
                      (do (rf nil) (seq (drain))))))))]
    (step inputs)))

(re-root! 'sequence
  (fn ([coll] (if (and (seq? coll) (not (object? coll))) coll (or (seq coll) ())))
    ([xform coll] (xf-sequence xform coll (fn [rf x] (rf nil x))))
    ([xform coll & colls]
     (xf-sequence xform (apply map vector coll colls) (fn [rf xs] (apply rf nil xs))))))

(re-root! 'pmap (fn [f & colls] (apply map f colls)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The names into clojure.core: seen by every namespace created after this one
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(doseq [[sym v] {'defprotocol #'defprotocol 'deftype #'deftype 'defrecord #'defrecord 'reify #'reify
                 'extend-type #'extend-type 'extend-protocol #'extend-protocol 'quote-or-value #'quote-or-value
                 'locking #'locking}]
  (intern 'clojure.core (with-meta sym {:macro true}) @v))
;; halt-when (clojure.core's transducer, which jank 0.1 lacks: measured — eve.thread.fold's rows name it)
(defn halt-when
  ([pred] (halt-when pred nil))
  ([pred retf]
   (fn [rf]
     (fn ([] (rf))
         ([result] (if (and (map? result) (contains? result ::halt)) (::halt result) (rf result)))
         ([result input] (if (pred input)
                           (reduced {::halt (if retf (retf (rf result) input) input)})
                           (rf result input)))))))

(doseq [[sym v] {'extend extend 'satisfies? satisfies? 'extends? extends? 'record? record?* 'halt-when halt-when
                 ;; Object as a value (instance?, extend, extends?): the name of every value's type
                 'Object 'Object}]
  (intern 'clojure.core sym v))

;; the printer's dynamic vars jank's core lacks (eve.vec's printer reads *print-length*): nil, Clojure's defaults
(doseq [sym '[*print-length* *print-level*]]
  (when-not (ns-resolve 'clojure.core sym)
    (intern 'clojure.core (with-meta sym {:dynamic true}) nil)))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The same names at ANALYSIS time (the AOT half). jank's AOT analyzer
;; resolves each module against the analyzer process's live clojure.core.
;; Load-time top-level forms never execute there, so the interns above are
;; invisible to dependent modules' analysis (measured: the whole-graph
;; compile dies at the first core call site, eve/atom.cljc's satisfies?).
;; But definitions made during one module's analysis ARE visible to modules
;; analyzed after it, and a macro's expansion is such a definition point
;; (measured in miniature: probe7/probe8, compiled-jank lane). This macro's
;; expansion performs exactly the interns the doseq forms above perform at
;; load; the doseqs remain the runtime half, binding the same roots when
;; this module's init runs -- on the JIT seat and in AOT binaries alike.
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defmacro aot-inject-core-names! []
  (doseq [[sym v] {'defprotocol #'defprotocol 'deftype #'deftype 'defrecord #'defrecord 'reify #'reify
                   'extend-type #'extend-type 'extend-protocol #'extend-protocol 'quote-or-value #'quote-or-value
                   'locking #'locking}]
    (intern 'clojure.core (with-meta sym {:macro true}) @v))
  (doseq [[sym v] {'extend extend 'satisfies? satisfies? 'extends? extends? 'record? record?* 'halt-when halt-when
                   'Object 'Object}]
    (intern 'clojure.core sym v))
  (doseq [sym '[*print-length* *print-level*]]
    (when-not (ns-resolve 'clojure.core sym)
      (intern 'clojure.core (with-meta sym {:dynamic true}) nil)))
  (intern 'clojure.core '->Eduction (fn [xform coll] (sequence xform coll)))
  (intern 'clojure.core 'eduction
          (fn ([xform coll] (sequence xform coll))
              ([xform coll & xforms] (sequence (apply comp xform xforms) coll))))
  (alter-meta! #'clojure.core/concat* dissoc :private)
  nil)

(aot-inject-core-names!)

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; load of a .cljc whose reader conditionals name :clj (F-JANK-LIBSPEC)
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; jank's reader features are #{:jank} only (measured: (quote #?(:clj :a :jank :b)) → :b, and
;; (quote [#?(:cljs cljs.reader :clj clojure.edn) :as edn]) → [:as edn] — an unmatched #? inside a
;; collection is dropped), so a vanilla .cljc written for the JVM/CLJS pair loses every :clj branch
;; at read time; in an ns libspec the lib name itself is destroyed and jank core's load-libs throws
;; "not a libspec: [:as edn]" (DataScript 1.8.1's datascript.core / datascript.query, byte-identical
;; upstream; contract-test six1-worker-jank3.log). The fix lives here, in the seat's completion:
;; clojure.core/load is re-rooted so that a module whose loaded source is a .cljc file is read form
;; by form through the runtime context's read_string with reader features #{:jank :clj} — jank's
;; own extended-features reader path (first matching branch in form order, :default as fallback,
;; :cljs never matches) — and evaluated form by form, which threads the ns switch exactly as a
;; file load does (measured). Every other module delegates to the original load untouched.
;; The ns form's :import clauses are stripped before eval: jank has no import ("`import` is not
;; supported in jank", measured); on the JVM an :import only creates hint aliases and there are
;; no classes here to alias. The port is never edited.
;; Second wall, same kind (found by the first proof run): the :clj face also requires modules
;; that exist only as .clj files (datascript.inline — clojure.lang.RT inlining shims;
;; datascript.pprint — java.io printing) and jank's loader has no .clj module type at all, so
;; those requires can never resolve here. process-ns-form below drops a :require clause whose
;; module is .clj-only on this host and un-excludes any referred name clojure.core provides
;; (datascript.inline/update → clojure.core/update, identical semantics); a module missing
;; outright keeps its clause and fails honestly.

(cpp/raw "
#include <jank/runtime/module/loader.hpp>
#include <jank/runtime/obj/persistent_string.hpp>
#include <cstdio>
#include <filesystem>
#include <fstream>
#include <iterator>
namespace eve_load {
  using namespace jank::runtime;
  /* cljc_source and loadable used to live here, calling module_loader.find.
     The AOT (static) runtime does not link that symbol -- a whole-graph
     `jank compile` reached the linker and failed on exactly those two
     references (measured, compiled-jank lane 2026-11-08). They are now
     answered in Clojure below, as a filesystem search over the same module
     path dirs (module-path-dirs), which is the search find performed.
     read_text_file is the one piece that stays native. */
  object_ref read_text_file(object_ref const path) {
    auto const p(expect_object<obj::persistent_string>(path)->data);
    std::ifstream in{ std::string(p.data(), p.size()), std::ios::binary };
    if(!in) { return jank_nil; }
    std::string const text{ std::istreambuf_iterator<char>(in), std::istreambuf_iterator<char>() };
    return make_box<obj::persistent_string>(jtl::immutable_string(text.data(), text.size()));
  }
  object_ref runtime_data() { return __rt_ctx->module_loader.to_runtime_data(); }
  /* flush: jank's core flush is a TODO stub (it throws after a println has
     already reached the fd); the completion re-roots it to a real flush of
     the C stdio stream every println writes through. */
  object_ref flush_stdout() { std::fflush(stdout); return jank_nil; }
  object_ref file_exists(object_ref const path) {
    auto const p(expect_object<obj::persistent_string>(path)->data);
    return make_box(std::filesystem::exists(std::filesystem::path{ std::string(p.data(), p.size()) }));
  }
}
")

(require '[clojure.string :as str])

;; (flush) is a TODO stub in jank's core (upstream defect 7): it throws ex-info "TODO: port flush" AFTER the
;; preceding println already reached stdout, which killed the translator's runs (compiled-jank lane) and ends
;; contract programs in a throw. Re-rooted to an fflush of stdout, the stream println writes through.
(re-root! 'flush (fn [] (cpp/eve_load.flush_stdout) nil))

(def ^:private orig-load load)
(def ^:private clj-feature-opts {:read-cond :allow :features #{:jank :clj}})
(def ^:private eve-loaded-modules (atom #{}))
(def ^:private eve-loading-modules (atom #{}))

(defn- load-module-name
  "The dotted module name for a load path, or nil when the path is relative (the original
   load resolves those against the current namespace; they delegate unchanged)."
  [path]
  (let [s (str path)]
    (cond (str/starts-with? s "/") (str/replace (subs s 1) "/" ".")
          (str/includes? s "/") nil
          :else s)))

(def ^:private module-path-dirs
  (delay (remove empty? (str/split (get (cpp/eve_load.runtime_data) "paths") #":"))))

(defn- module-rel-path
  "The module-path-relative source path stem for a dotted module name."
  [module]
  (str/replace (str/replace module "." "/") "-" "_"))

(defn- find-on-module-path
  "The first module-path file for module with one of exts, or nil. Path
   entries that are JAR/ZIP archives are not searched -- the seat's module
   paths are plain directories."
  [module exts]
  (let [rel (module-rel-path module)]
    (some (fn [dir]
            (some (fn [ext]
                    (let [p (str dir "/" rel ext)]
                      (when (cpp/eve_load.file_exists p) p)))
                  exts))
          @module-path-dirs)))

(defn- loadable
  "True when the module path holds a source the loader could load for module
   (a .cljc, .jank or .cpp file, in path order). The C++ original asked
   module_loader.find, which the AOT runtime does not link; this is the same
   filesystem search over the same dirs. A module present only as a compiled
   object reads as not-loadable here -- module-state's callers only
   distinguish source modules, which is what the distinction is for."
  [module]
  (some? (find-on-module-path module [".cljc" ".jank" ".cpp"])))

(defn- cljc-source
  "The source text of module's .cljc file on the module path, or nil when the
   module has no filesystem .cljc source (a .jank/.cpp/baked module, or not
   found) -- the C++ original's contract, answered without
   module_loader.find."
  [module]
  (when-let [p (find-on-module-path module [".cljc"])]
    (cpp/eve_load.read_text_file p)))

(defn- module-state
  "\"loadable\" when the loader can load the module; \"clj-only\" when it exists on the
   module path only as a .clj file (a JVM-host module — jank's loader has no .clj
   module type and does not index them); \"missing\" otherwise."
  [module]
  (cond (loadable module) "loadable"
        (let [rel (str (str/replace (str/replace module "." "/") "-" "_") ".clj")]
          (some (fn [dir] (cpp/eve_load.file_exists (str dir "/" rel))) @module-path-dirs)) "clj-only"
        :else "missing"))

(defn- simple-libspec?
  "A libspec naming one lib directly: a symbol, or a vector whose head is the lib and whose
   second element (when present) is an option keyword. Prefix lists are not simple."
  [spec]
  (or (symbol? spec)
      (and (vector? spec) (symbol? (first spec))
           (or (= 1 (count spec)) (keyword? (second spec))))))

(defn- libspec-referred
  "The var names a libspec refers ([] when it refers none, or :all)."
  [spec]
  (if (vector? spec)
    (let [opts (apply hash-map (drop 1 spec))]
      (if (contains? opts :refer)
        (let [r (:refer opts)] (if (= :all r) :all (vec r)))
        []))
    []))

(defn- process-ns-form
  "An ns form made loadable on this host, without touching the library's source:
   - :refer-clojure clauses move ahead of the other reference clauses (jank's ns macro
     processes references in source order; JVM Clojure refers clojure.core first).
   - :import clauses are dropped (jank cannot honor them; see the section head).
   - A :require clause naming a module that exists only as a .clj file — a JVM-host
     module jank's loader cannot load (datascript.inline, datascript.pprint) — is
     dropped, and any var it referred that clojure.core also provides is removed
     from the :refer-clojure :exclude list, so the core var serves instead. The
     :clj face of a vanilla library uses such modules as JVM shims (inline is
     clojure.lang.RT inlining; the semantics are core's); a module that is missing
     outright keeps its clause, so the load fails with the honest error."
  [form]
  (if-not (and (seq? form) (= 'ns (first form)))
    form
    (let [clauses (drop 2 form)
          ;; jank's ns macro processes reference clauses in source order; JVM Clojure applies
          ;; :refer-clojure before the other references. A vanilla ns form that puts
          ;; (:refer-clojure ...) after (:require ...) (DataScript's shape) would otherwise run
          ;; its requires in a namespace clojure.core has not been referred into yet, and a
          ;; not-yet-loaded .jank module's own (ns ...) head then fails to resolve. Move the
          ;; :refer-clojure clauses ahead of the other reference clauses; any docstring /
          ;; attr-map (non-seq heads) keep their place at the front.
          [head-clauses ref-clauses] (split-with (complement seq?) clauses)
          ordered-clauses (concat head-clauses
                                  (filter (fn [c] (= :refer-clojure (first c))) ref-clauses)
                                  (remove (fn [c] (= :refer-clojure (first c))) ref-clauses))
          dropped-refers
          (into []
                (comp (filter (fn [c] (and (seq? c) (= :require (first c)))))
                      (mapcat (fn [c] (rest c)))
                      (filter (fn [spec] (and (simple-libspec? spec)
                                              (= "clj-only" (module-state (str (if (vector? spec) (first spec) spec)))))))
                      (mapcat (fn [spec] (let [r (libspec-referred spec)] (if (= :all r) [] r))))
                      (filter (fn [sym] (ns-resolve 'clojure.core sym))))
                clauses)
          dropped (set dropped-refers)]
      (apply list (first form) (second form)
             (mapcat (fn [clause]
                       (cond (not (seq? clause)) [clause]
                             (= :import (first clause)) []
                             (= :require (first clause))
                             [(apply list :require
                                     (remove (fn [spec] (and (simple-libspec? spec)
                                                              (= "clj-only" (module-state (str (if (vector? spec) (first spec) spec))))))
                                             (rest clause)))]
                             (and (= :refer-clojure (first clause)) (seq dropped))
                             [(concat (list :refer-clojure)
                                      (mapcat (fn [[k v]] (if (= :exclude k)
                                                            [k (vec (remove dropped v))]
                                                            [k v]))
                                              (partition 2 (rest clause))))]
                             :else [clause]))
                     ordered-clauses)))))

(defn- eval-cljc-source!
  "Read src's forms with :clj among the reader features and eval each in order.
   Forms live at read_string indices 1..N; a nil read is the end of the source."
  [src]
  (loop [n 1]
    (let [form (cpp/.read_string cpp/jank.runtime.__rt_ctx src clj-feature-opts n)]
      (when (some? form)
        (eval (clj-face (process-ns-form form)))
        (recur (inc n))))))

(def ^:private translated-tree?
  "True when a module-path dir carries the `.eve-translated` marker that
   scripts/compiled-jank/stage-translate.sh writes into the mirror tree it
   builds: every .cljc there IS this loader's translation already (reader
   conditionals resolved, clj-face applied, ns forms made loadable), so
   jank's own load reads it -- and under `jank compile`, compiles it. With
   this override active over such a tree, every .cljc require was
   JIT-evaluated by eval-cljc-source! instead (measured 2026-11-09,
   compiled-jank lane: the build's cache held 17 .o files, all .jank
   modules, none of the graph's .cljc, and the entry's graph died in the
   JIT path), so the translated tree names itself and eve-load steps aside."
  (delay (boolean (some (fn [dir] (cpp/eve_load.file_exists (str dir "/.eve-translated")))
                        @module-path-dirs))))

(declare eve-load-cljc)

(defn- eve-load [& paths]
  (if @translated-tree?
    (apply orig-load paths)
    (apply eve-load-cljc paths)))

(defn- eve-load-cljc [& paths]
  (doseq [path paths]
    (let [module (load-module-name path)]
      (if (nil? module)
        (orig-load path)
        (let [src (when-not (contains? @eve-loaded-modules module)
                    (cljc-source module))]
          (cond (nil? src) (orig-load path)
                (contains? @eve-loading-modules module)
                (throw (ex-info (str "Cyclic load dependency: " module) {:module module}))
                :else (do (swap! eve-loading-modules conj module)
                          (try ;; load_module restores *ns* when a module is loaded; the eval
                               ;; loop must give load's caller the same contract, or an outer
                               ;; ns form's remaining refer/alias steps — and its body forms —
                               ;; resolve in the loaded library's namespace instead of its own
                               ;; (measured: eve.mem's extend-default, referred from eve.host,
                               ;; unresolved after eve.deftype-proto.data loaded through here).
                               (binding [*ns* *ns*]
                                 (eval-cljc-source! src))
                               (swap! eve-loaded-modules conj module)
                               (finally (swap! eve-loading-modules disj module))))))))))

(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/load (fn [_] eve-load))

;; jank's reader expands a splicing syntax-quote (`x ~@ys`) into a call to clojure.core/concat*,
;; clojure.core's bootstrap concat — private as a bootstrap detail, but named by reader-emitted
;; code in any namespace, whose analysis jank then refuses ("The var `clojure.core/concat*` is
;; private": measured, Lane M 2026-11-06, on datascript.util's log/raise macros). Eve's own code
;; avoids ~@ for this (the types adapter builds forms with list*); vanilla code cannot be asked
;; to. The completion answers it the way JVM Clojure's reader behaves — there the emitted name is
;; the public concat: the privacy flag on the reader-named var is dropped.
(alter-meta! #'clojure.core/concat* dissoc :private)

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; The :clj-face shims clj-face's translations call: the exception classes are
;; ex-info; an ArrayList is a transient vector being built (its .add is conj!,
;; answering true as List.add does); List.get/Map.get are one read (a numeric
;; key indexes, any other looks up); Writer.write prints to the writer bound
;; as *out*; a UUID is its two longs, [msb lsb] — compared and hashed by
;; content, as a UUID is.
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(defn ex-info-ctor
  "An exception class of the :clj face (IllegalArgumentException, UnsupportedOperationException,
   Exception) built as the seat's throwable: ex-info with the message, or no message."
  ([] (ex-info "" {}))
  ([msg] (ex-info (str msg) {}))
  ([msg _cause] (ex-info (str msg) {})))

(defn array-list
  "java.util.ArrayList, as a transient vector under construction (the capacity hint is read and dropped)."
  [& _]
  (transient []))

(defn jvm-add
  "List.add on the ArrayList shim: conj!, answering true as List.add does."
  [t x]
  (conj! t x)
  true)

(defn jvm-get
  "List.get / Map.get: a numeric key indexes the target, any other key looks it up."
  [t k]
  (if (number? k) (nth t k) (get t k)))

(defn jvm-write
  "Writer.write: print s to the writer, as *out*."
  [w s]
  (binding [*out* w] (print (str s)))
  nil)

(defn print-via-string-writer
  "print-method's defn on this seat, for (defmethod print-method T [x w] body...): the method
   runs against a string writer (the encoding adapter's string-writer, loaded here on first
   use — this namespace loads before it exists) and what it wrote is the instance's printed
   form. body keeps its own names: [x w] is the method's argument vector as written."
  [x args body]
  (let [w ((ns-resolve (do (require (quote eve.encoding)) (find-ns (quote eve.encoding)))
                       (quote string-writer)))
        f (eval (list 'fn args body))]
    (f x w)
    (str (deref w))))

(defn uuid-new
  "java.util.UUID as its two longs: [msb lsb]."
  [msb lsb]
  [msb lsb])

(defn uuid-msb [u] (nth u 0))
(defn uuid-lsb [u] (nth u 1))

(defn- rand-long []
  (bit-or (bit-shift-left (rand-int 2147483647) 32)
          (bit-and (rand-int 2147483647) 0xffffffff)))

(when-not (find-ns 'UUID)
  (create-ns 'UUID)
  (intern 'UUID 'randomUUID (fn [] (uuid-new (rand-long) (rand-long)))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; System/*: the JVM class-statics vanilla code calls by name — identityHashCode
;; (datascript.impl.entity's hash-entity), getProperty (datascript.util's log
;; macro, at expansion time), currentTimeMillis (datascript.util's squuid).
;; There is no System class here; a namespace of that name carrying the vars
;; answers the same symbols. Each answer is the honest one for this host: the
;; instance's own address is its identity hash; no system properties are set
;; (getProperty answers nil, or the caller's default); the wall clock is real.
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(when-not (find-ns 'System)
  (create-ns 'System)
  (intern 'System 'identityHashCode (fn [x] (bit-and (object-addr x) 0x7fffffff)))
  (intern 'System 'getProperty (fn ([_] nil) ([_ d] d)))
  (intern 'System 'currentTimeMillis (fn [] (cpp/eve_host.now_millis))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; Math/*: the JVM class-statics vanilla code names (datascript.built-ins'
;; aggregate-stddev calls Math/sqrt as a function value). There is no Math
;; class here; a namespace of that name carrying the vars answers the same
;; symbols, in call position and in value position alike. The answers are
;; the host's own scalar math (cpp/*) and core's min/max/abs.
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

(when-not (find-ns 'Math)
  (create-ns 'Math)
  (intern 'Math 'sqrt (fn [x] (cpp/sqrt (double x))))
  (intern 'Math 'pow (fn [x y] (cpp/pow (double x) (double y))))
  (intern 'Math 'floor (fn [x] (cpp/floor (double x))))
  (intern 'Math 'ceil (fn [x] (cpp/ceil (double x))))
  (intern 'Math 'exp (fn [x] (cpp/exp (double x))))
  (intern 'Math 'log (fn [x] (cpp/log (double x))))
  (intern 'Math 'sin (fn [x] (cpp/sin (double x))))
  (intern 'Math 'cos (fn [x] (cpp/cos (double x))))
  (intern 'Math 'tan (fn [x] (cpp/tan (double x))))
  (intern 'Math 'abs (fn [x] (if (neg? x) (- x) x)))
  (intern 'Math 'min (fn [x y] (min x y)))
  (intern 'Math 'max (fn [x y] (max x y))))

;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; (refer 'clojure.core), the one every ns form expands to
;; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
;; jank's refer rebuilds ns-publics of clojure.core (a reduce over its whole mapping, core.jank:4640) and refers each
;; var through a Clojure reduce, per namespace created. Unfiltered, of clojure.core: the publics are kept while
;; clojure.core's mapping is the same map (identical?: a name interned into clojure.core makes a new one), and the
;; refers run in eve_host::refer_all. Every other call is jank's own.
(def ^:private core-refer (deref #'clojure.core/refer))
(def ^:private core-publics
  "[clojure.core's mapping, its publics] of the last unfiltered (refer 'clojure.core)."
  (atom nil))
(defn- clojure-core-publics []
  (let [ns (the-ns 'clojure.core)
        m (cpp/jank.runtime.ns_map ns)
        c (cpp/jank.runtime.deref core-publics)]
    (if (and c (identical? m (nth c 0)))
      (nth c 1)
      (let [p (ns-publics ns)] (reset! core-publics [m p]) p))))
(alter-var-root #'clojure.core/refer
  (fn [_] (fn [ns-sym & filters]
            (if (and (nil? filters) (= 'clojure.core ns-sym))
              (cpp/eve_host.refer_all *ns* (clojure-core-publics))
              (apply core-refer ns-sym filters)))))
